CET.data.listeningByYear[2020] = [{"id":"L2","level":"CET4","type":"短对话","source":"2020年9月 · 四级 · 短对话","year":2020,"session":"9月","title":"改签火车票","intro":"女士因会议延时错过原班火车，在窗口改签并挑选座位。","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet4-2020-09-set1.mp3","lines":[{"sp":"Q1","en":"A NASA satellite orbiting over Portugal took photographs that reveal the effects of pollution from ships.","cn":"NASA一颗在葡萄牙上空运行的卫星拍摄的照片揭示了船舶污染的影响。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"One of the photos shows a thin film of clouds above the brilliant blue of the North Atlantic, cut by white lines of thicker clouds that look like scars.","cn":"其中一张照片显示,在北大西洋耀眼的蓝色上方有一层薄薄的云,被看起来像伤疤的白色粗云线条切割开来。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"NASA officials explained those thicker clouds are signs of ship traffic below.","cn":"NASA官员解释说,那些较厚的云是下方船舶交通的迹象。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"When ships power their way through the ocean, they pump exhaust into the atmosphere, just as cars do.","cn":"当船舶在海洋中航行时,它们会像汽车一样向大气中排放废气。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"And those massive amounts of particles can cause clouds to form.","cn":"而那些大量的颗粒物会导致云的形成。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Get enough of those particles in one place, as from the exhaust of a ship, and they can lead to the creation of new clouds easily visible from space.","cn":"当足够多的这些颗粒物聚集在一个地方,比如来自船舶的废气,它们就会导致新云层的形成,从太空中很容易看到。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"\"These clouds can be huge.","cn":"NASA官员说:'这些云可能非常巨大。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Some of them stretch hundreds of kilometres from end to end,\" NASA officials said.","cn":"其中一些从一端到另一端绵延数百公里。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"It's likely that these sorts of clouds are having some effect on the global climate, according to NASA officials.","cn":"'据NASA官员称,这类云很可能对全球气候产生某种影响。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"But scientists aren't yet sure what effect it has.","cn":"但科学家们还不确定它会产生什么影响。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"Staff at a suburban supermarket in Melbourne say they feel unsafe at work after security guards were removed.","cn":"Melbourne郊区一家超市的员工表示，在保安人员被撤走后，他们感到工作不安全。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"This came after a series of physical attacks and verbal abuse by customers.","cn":"此前发生了一系列顾客对员工的肢体攻击和言语辱骂事件。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"More than 50 workers at the store have signed a letter calling for a permanent security guard following a series of incidents, including a customer threatening to attack a supervisor with a knife.","cn":"该店超过50名员工签署了一封信函，要求配备常驻保安，此前发生了一系列事件,包括一名顾客威胁要用刀攻击一名主管。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"A security worker had guarded the store each night from 7 p.m. until 12 a.m., but that had stopped suddenly on Monday, employees said.","cn":"员工称，此前每晚7点到午夜12点都有一名保安值守，但这一安排在周一突然停止了。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"One worker said an angry customer had thrown a chicken at his head after complaining about how long she had waited to be served.","cn":"一名员工说，一位愤怒的顾客在抱怨等待服务时间过长后，向他头部扔了一只鸡。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"Another worker said the lack of protection at the store made her feel uncomfortable at work.","cn":"另一名员工表示，店内缺乏保护措施让她在工作时感到不安。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"However, the spokesman of the supermarket said the store had taken strong action in response to incidents.","cn":"然而，该超市的发言人表示，店方已对这些事件采取了强有力的应对措施。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"\"We have found very few instances of bad customer behavior at our store in the past year.","cn":"\"我们发现过去一年中本店极少出现顾客不当行为。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"In the rare cases we have seen bad behavior, we have taken strong action in response, including banning a customer from the store.\"","cn":"在我们遇到的罕见不当行为案例中，我们都采取了强有力的应对措施，包括禁止某位顾客进入本店。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Drivers on their way to the Polish capital of Warsaw on Wednesday morning found the road blocked by an unusual obstacle: tons of liquid chocolate that spilled onto the motorway.","cn":"周三上午，前往波兰首都华沙的司机们发现道路被一个不寻常的障碍物堵住了：数吨液体巧克力洒在了高速公路上。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"A truck carrying the sweet load hit a road barrier and overturned, blocking two lanes.","cn":"一辆装载着这些甜蜜货物的卡车撞上了道路护栏并侧翻,堵塞了两条车道。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"The cracked tank spilled a pool of rapidly-hardening chocolate, which quickly covered the width of the road.","cn":"破裂的储罐溢出了一大片迅速凝固的巧克力,很快覆盖了整个路面宽度。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"While the driver was taken to hospital with a broken arm, firefighters struggled to remove a reported twelve tons of solid chocolate from the road.","cn":"司机因手臂骨折被送往医院,而消防员则艰难地清除路面上据报道有十二吨的固体巧克力。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"A representative for the firefighters told the local TV that removing the chocolate was worse than dealing with snow.","cn":"消防队的一名代表告诉当地电视台,清除巧克力比处理积雪还要困难。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"After contacting the chocolate manufacturer, the firefighters resorted to spraying hot, pressurized water to get rid of the sticky substance.","cn":"在联系了巧克力制造商后,消防员采取了喷洒热的高压水来清除这种黏性物质。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"The local TV also noted that the cleanup spanned more than a mile, because drivers simply drove through the chocolate after the crash, leaving a long chocolate trail.","cn":"当地电视台还指出,清理工作跨越了一英里多,因为事故发生后司机们直接开车穿过巧克力,留下了一条长长的巧克力痕迹。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But despite the sticky situation, firefighters and police attending to the cleanup were reportedly cheerful about the long task ahead.","cn":"但尽管情况棘手,据报道参与清理工作的消防员和警察对眼前的漫长任务都很乐观。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"After all, who could be mad about twelve tons of chocolate?","cn":"毕竟,谁会因为十二吨巧克力而生气呢?"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: Lisa, why did you pay for your meal with cash instead of the payment apps on your phone?","cn":"M: Lisa,你为什么用现金付餐费,而不是用手机上的支付应用?"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: Well, I've gone back to cash.","cn":"W: 嗯,我已经改回用现金了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I'm only using payment apps if that's the only option.","cn":"只有在别无选择的情况下我才用支付应用。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I'm trying to save money for a new phone, and I find that using cash rather than payment apps helps me to save.","cn":"我想攒钱买个新手机,我发现用现金而不是支付应用能帮我省钱。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: But how?","cn":"M: 但怎么会呢?钱就是钱,不是吗?我觉得不管你是从银行取出来放进钱包,还是用应用从你的银行账户转到卖家的银行账户,都没什么区别。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"Money is money, isn't it?","cn":""},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I don't think it matters whether you take it out to the bank and put it in your wallet or simply transfer from your bank account to the seller's bank account using an app.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: No, I believe it does matter.","cn":"W: 不,我认为确实有区别。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"It's a psychological phenomenon.","cn":"这是一种心理现象。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I believe we have less connection with the value of our money when we just tap the \"Approve\" buttons on our phones.","cn":"我觉得当我们只是在手机上点\"确认\"按钮时,我们和钱的价值之间的联系就少了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: You might have a point.","cn":"M: 你说得有道理。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"Since I stopped carrying cash around and started using my phone apps to pay, I may have developed a tendency to buy more small or non-essential items.","cn":"自从我不再随身带现金,开始用手机应用支付以后,我可能养成了更多购买小件或非必需品的倾向。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: That's highly possible.","cn":"W: 很有可能。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"Think about the amount of time we spend with our phones in our hands, and all the things we do with our phones.","cn":"想想我们手里拿着手机的时间有多长,还有我们用手机做的所有事情。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"It sometimes seems that our phone is buying the product for us, not ourselves.","cn":"有时候感觉好像是我们的手机在买东西,而不是我们自己。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: So cashless payment affects our ability to budget?","cn":"M: 所以无现金支付影响我们做预算的能力?"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: I believe so.","cn":"W: 我认为是的。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"If we spend a hundred yuan in cash, we realize that we don't have that hundred yuan to spend on something else.","cn":"如果我们花了一百元现金,我们会意识到我们没有那一百元去花在别的东西上了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"But if we're spending electronically, we are less likely to make that mental calculation.","cn":"但如果我们是电子支付,我们就不太可能做那种心理计算。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: I stopped using my credit card because I found I was spending excessively.","cn":"M: 我不用信用卡了,因为我发现我花得太多。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"Perhaps I should take the same approach of paying using my phone.","cn":"也许我应该对手机支付采取同样的做法。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: It's worth considering.","cn":"W: 值得考虑。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Hello, Mr. Brown.","cn":"W: 您好，Brown先生。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I was expecting your call.","cn":"我一直在等您的电话。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"My secretary told me you were having some problems with the wooden table.","cn":"我的秘书告诉我您那张木桌子出了些问题。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Is that right?","cn":"是这样吗？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: No, no.","cn":"M: 不不不。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The table is fine.","cn":"桌子没问题。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The problem is the chairs.","cn":"问题出在椅子上。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Oh, the chairs.","cn":"W: 哦，椅子。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"So what exactly is the issue?","cn":"那具体是什么问题呢？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Well, put simply, these are not the chairs my wife and I selected in your store last week.","cn":"M: 嗯，简单来说，这些椅子不是我和我妻子上周在你们店里选的那些。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"There must be some confusion with our order.","cn":"我们的订单肯定搞混了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Oh, I see.","cn":"W: 哦，我明白了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I'm looking through my files now, and I see that the delivery was this morning.","cn":"我现在正在查我的文件，我看到送货是今天早上。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Is that correct?","cn":"对吗？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Yes.","cn":"M: 是的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Do you mind describing the chairs that were delivered to your apartment, Mr. Brown?","cn":"W: Brown先生，您介意描述一下送到您公寓的那些椅子吗？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Sure.","cn":"M: 当然可以。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"These have a flat back with a rounded top and are very heavy.","cn":"这些椅子是平背的，顶部是圆的，而且非常重。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"They are light brown and look kind of cheap.","cn":"它们是浅棕色的，看起来有点廉价。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The ones we ordered were dark brown to match the table.","cn":"我们订的那些是深棕色的，要和桌子配套。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Right, of course.","cn":"W: 好的，当然。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"It says here you purchased the Arlington table and four Milano chairs.","cn":"这里显示您购买的是Arlington桌子和四把Milano椅子。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"As you said, there must have been some confusion with the order.","cn":"正如您所说，订单肯定搞混了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I'm terribly sorry.","cn":"非常抱歉。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"We will send a van to collect those four and replace them with the Milano you purchased.","cn":"我们会派车去收回那四把椅子，换成您购买的Milano椅子。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Will tomorrow 9 a.m. be okay, Mr. Brown?","cn":"明天早上9点可以吗，Brown先生？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Yes, that would be great.","cn":"M: 可以，那太好了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Thank you.","cn":"谢谢您。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Good.","cn":"W: 好的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Did everything else you ordered from us arrive okay?","cn":"您从我们这订的其他东西都到齐了吗？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Yes, I think so.","cn":"M: 是的，我想是的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Let me check.","cn":"让我检查一下。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The mirror and two paintings are here.","cn":"镜子和两幅画在这儿。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The two coffee tables are also here.","cn":"两张茶几也在这儿。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"And the sofa… Yes, we haven't noticed anything else wrong or missing.","cn":"还有沙发……是的，我们没注意到有其他东西不对或缺失。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"But if we do, we will certainly let you know.","cn":"但如果有的话，我们一定会告诉您。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Okay, great.","cn":"W: 好的，太好了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Once again, I'm sorry for the confusion and trouble caused.","cn":"再次为造成的混乱和麻烦向您道歉。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Do you have too much stuff?","cn":"你是否拥有太多东西？你是否，容我直言，\"不整洁\"？来认识一下一档名为《跟着Marie Kondo学整理》的电视节目，这是一档基于她极受欢迎的书籍《怦然心动的人生整理魔法》的家居改造节目。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Are you, dare we say it \"untidy\"?","cn":"在节目中，Marie Kondo扮演着凌乱之人的小小垃圾仙子，造访他们的房屋以分享\"KonMari\"方法的智慧。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Say hello to a TV show called \"Tidying Up with Marie Kondo\", a home improvement show based on her wildly popular book The Life-Changing Magic of Tidying Up.","cn":"这个方法在理论上很简单,但在实践中可能无限复杂。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"In the show, Marie Kondo acts as a tiny garbage fairy for messy people, visiting their houses to share the wisdom of the \"KonMari\" method.","cn":"你要把家里的所有东西——所有东西——分成几个类别,然后检查每一件物品——每一件——看它是否能激发喜悦。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"This method is simple in theory but can be endlessly complex in practice.","cn":"如果能,你就保留它。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"You divide all the stuff in your house—all of it—into several categories, and then examine each item—all of them—to see if it sparks joy.","cn":"如果不能,你就感谢它并整齐地丢弃它。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"If it does, you keep it.","cn":"那么,这档电视节目是否激励人们去整理呢?第一手资料似乎表明出现了一小波人们将成堆的捐赠袋带到二手商店的浪潮。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"If it doesn't, you thank it and neatly discard it.","cn":"一家商店在一天内收到了数千袋二手物品。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"So, is the TV show inspiring people to tidy up?","cn":"一月通常是这些商店捐赠的淡季,因为天气寒冷,人们不想费事,但今年一月不同。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Firsthand accounts seem to indicate a small wave of people bringing piles of donation bags to used goods stores.","cn":"人们似乎下定决心清理他们的家。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"One store received thousands of bags of used possessions in one day.","cn":"一家二手书店在一周内收到了相当于一个月的捐赠书籍,当时一名男子从家里捐出了五十多箱书。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"January is usually the stores' slow season for donations because it's cold and people don't want to bother, but not this January.","cn":"看来Marie的电视节目毕竟产生了巨大影响。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"People seemed determined to clean up their homes.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q16","en":"One used bookstore received a month's worth of books in donations in a week when a man gave over fifty boxes of books from his home.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It seems Marie's TV show is having a big impact after all.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q19","en":"At just 12 years old, Mike Hannon is making a difference in his community one lunch at a time.","cn":"年仅12岁的Mike Hannon正在通过一份份午餐为他的社区带来改变。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"\"Mike's Lunches of Love\" has fed more than 2,000 of the town's most vulnerable residents.","cn":"\"Mike的爱心午餐\"已经为镇上2000多名最脆弱的居民提供了食物。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Mike delivers meals to the homeless.","cn":"Mike为无家可归者送餐。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"\"It's like a way to give people joy, maybe spark something in them that can change them,\" Mike told WBZ-TV.","cn":"\"这就像是给人们带来快乐的一种方式，也许能在他们心中点燃某种可以改变他们的东西，\"Mike告诉WBZ-TV。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The mayor of Mike's town feels that Mike is a great community leader, especially in such times of so much negative news.","cn":"Mike所在镇的镇长认为Mike是一位优秀的社区领袖，尤其是在充斥着如此多负面新闻的时期。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"While his father commented on how proud he was of his son, yet, Mike isn't looking for praise, but kindness in return.","cn":"他的父亲评论说他为儿子感到多么自豪，然而Mike并不是在寻求赞扬，而是希望得到善意的回报。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"He hopes his acts of charity will influence others to spread positive actions in their own towns.","cn":"他希望自己的慈善行为能影响其他人在他们自己的城镇传播积极的行动。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Mike includes a handwritten message of joy on each bag.","cn":"Mike在每个袋子上都附有一条手写的快乐留言。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"His message and star power have spread all over the country.","cn":"他的留言和明星影响力已经传遍全国。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"To date, his online page to raise funds has brought in more than $44,000 and counting, raising more than $17,000 in just one day, with the help of many famous actors and others.","cn":"迄今为止，他的在线筹款页面已经筹集了超过44000美元并且还在增加，仅一天就筹集了超过17000美元，这得益于许多著名演员和其他人的帮助。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"People from all over the country are sending special handcrafted bags to help the young man with his mission to help those in need.","cn":"来自全国各地的人们正在寄送特制的手工袋子，以帮助这位年轻人完成帮助需要帮助的人的使命。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Many are hoping the simple act of kindness spreads.","cn":"许多人希望这种简单的善举能够传播开来。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Mike is seen as hope for the future of the town, the country and the world.","cn":"Mike被视为该镇、该国和世界未来的希望。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In a recent study carried out by psychologists on the disruptive effects of smartphones, two groups of college students were given word search puzzles.","cn":"在心理学家最近开展的一项关于智能手机干扰效应的研究中,两组大学生被要求完成单词搜索谜题。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The first group was told to complete the puzzles with its participants' smartphones in their line of sight.","cn":"第一组被告知在参与者视线范围内有智能手机的情况下完成谜题。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The second group, however, was told that the phones would interfere with the equipment in the experiment, and would need to be moved away from the testing area.","cn":"然而,第二组被告知手机会干扰实验设备,需要移到测试区域之外。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Midway through the second group's solving of the puzzles, the experimenter called one of the phones and let it ring for a while before hanging up.","cn":"在第二组解谜题进行到一半时,实验人员拨打了其中一部手机,让它响了一会儿后才挂断。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Many of the students in that group were unable to focus from then on, becoming anxious and performing more poorly than the first group.","cn":"该组中许多学生从那时起无法集中注意力,变得焦虑,表现也比第一组差。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Use of electronics has also been known to lead to a decline in human interactions.","cn":"电子产品的使用也被认为会导致人际互动的减少。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Rather than having real-life conversations, many express emotions and engage in deep conversations through social media sites.","cn":"许多人不是进行现实生活中的对话,而是通过社交媒体网站表达情感和进行深入交流。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Many students use their phones and computers during class for non-academic activities, which leads to poor grades.","cn":"许多学生在课堂上将手机和电脑用于非学术活动,这导致成绩不佳。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Perhaps the most dramatic impact is the reduction in the amount of sleep, which leads to poor health and weight gain.","cn":"也许最显著的影响是睡眠时间的减少,这会导致健康状况不佳和体重增加。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Technology is a great tool; however, it's important to recognize its downsides.","cn":"技术是一个伟大的工具;然而,认识到它的缺点很重要。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Lack of sleep, reduction of productivity and weight gain are only a few.","cn":"睡眠不足、生产力下降和体重增加只是其中几个问题。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"If we're not careful about all these minor problems right now, the effect on the future generation is going to be much bigger.","cn":"如果我们现在不注意所有这些小问题,对未来一代的影响将会大得多。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why does the woman need to change her ticket?","options":["She missed her original train","She wants to travel with a friend","Her train was cancelled","She prefers a later arrival time"],"answer":0,"explain":"女士说会议比预想的长，而原票是一点十五的车、现在已经过两点，说明她错过了原来那趟车。"},{"q":"How much extra does she have to pay?","options":["Twenty yuan","Twelve yuan","Ten yuan","Nothing"],"answer":0,"explain":"售票员说 you will have to pay the difference of twenty yuan，需要补二十元差价。"},{"q":"What seat does she finally get?","options":["A window seat","An aisle seat near the front","A seat in the dining car","A first class seat"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 I can give you an aisle seat near the front，女士也接受了走道边的座位。"}],"cloze":[{"text":"I would like to ______ my ticket to the 3:30 train to Shanghai.","answers":["change"],"hint":"改签、更改"},{"text":"My meeting ran longer than I ______.","answers":["expected"],"hint":"预料、预期"},{"text":"The train ______ in at 6:05.","answers":["gets"],"hint":"到达（get in）"}]},{"id":"L7","level":"CET6","type":"讲座","source":"2020年9月 · 六级 · 讲座","year":2020,"session":"9月","title":"睡眠如何巩固记忆","intro":"讲座阐述睡眠如何巩固白天所学，以及睡眠不足带来的影响。","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet6-2020-09-set1.mp3","lines":[{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: You are a professor of physics at the University of Oxford.","cn":"M: 您是牛津大学的物理学教授，也是欧洲核子研究组织的高级顾问。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"You're a senior advisor at the European Organization for Nuclear Research.","cn":"您似乎还在不停地周游世界，发表演讲。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"You also seem to tour the globe tirelessly, giving talks.","cn":"此外，您还有自己的每周科学电视节目。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"And in addition, you have your own weekly TV show on science.","cn":"您哪儿来的这么多精力？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Where do you get the energy?","cn":""},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Oh, well, I just love what I do.","cn":"W: 哦，是这样，我就是热爱自己所做的事情。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I'm extremely fortunate to have this life, doing what I love doing.","cn":"我非常幸运，能够过着这样的生活，做自己喜欢做的事。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Professor, what exactly is your goal?","cn":"M: 教授，您的目标究竟是什么？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Why do you do all of these?","cn":"您为什么要做这一切？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Well, as you said, I do have different things going on.","cn":"W: 嗯，正如您所说，我确实同时在做不同的事情。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"But these, I think, can be divided into two groups: the education of science and the further understanding of science.","cn":"但我认为，这些事情可以分为两类：科学教育和进一步理解科学。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Don't these two things get in the way of each other?","cn":"M: 这两件事不会互相妨碍吗？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"What I mean is, doesn't giving lectures take time away from the lab?","cn":"我的意思是，发表演讲不会占用您在实验室里的时间吗？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Not really, no.","cn":"W: 不会，确实不会。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I love teaching, and I don't mind spending more time doing that now than in the past.","cn":"我喜欢教学，而且现在比过去多花些时间做这件事，我也不介意。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Also, what I will say is that teaching a subject helps me comprehend it better myself.","cn":"另外，我想说的是，教授一门学科有助于我自己更好地理解它。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I find that it furthers my own knowledge when I have to explain something clearly, when I have to aid others in understanding it, and when I have to answer questions about it.","cn":"当我必须清楚地解释某件事、帮助别人理解它，以及回答有关它的问题时，我发现自己的知识也会因此得到拓展。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Teaching at a high level can be very stimulating for anyone, no matter how much expertise they may already have in the field they are instructing.","cn":"无论一个人在所教授的领域中已经有多么丰富的专业知识，高水平的教学都能对他产生很大的启发。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Are there any scientific breakthroughs that you see on the near horizon, a significant discovery or invention we can expect soon?","cn":"M: 您认为近期会出现什么科学突破吗？比如我们很快就能期待的重大​​发现或发明？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: The world is always conducting science, and there are constantly new things being discovered.","cn":"W: 世界各地一直都在进行科学研究，不断有新事物被发现。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"In fact, right now we have too much data sitting in computers.","cn":"事实上，我们现在有太多数据堆积在电脑里了。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"For example, we have thousands of photos of planet Mars taken by telescopes that nobody has ever seen.","cn":"比如，望远镜拍摄了数千张火星的照片，却从来没有人看过。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"We have them, yet nobody has had time to look at them with their own eyes, let alone analyze them.","cn":"照片是有的，但还没有人有时间亲眼查看，更不用说分析它们了。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Do you think dreams have special meanings?","cn":"M: 你觉得梦有特殊的含义吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: No, I don't think they do.","cn":"W: 不，我不这么认为。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: I don't either.","cn":"M: 我也不这么认为。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But some people do.","cn":"不过有些人确实这么想。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"I would say people who believe that dreams have special meanings are superstitious, especially nowadays.","cn":"我会说，相信梦有特殊含义的人很迷信，尤其是在如今这个时代。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"In the past, during the times of ancient Egypt, Greece or China, people used to believe that dreams could foresee the future.","cn":"过去，在古埃及、古希腊或古代中国，人们曾经相信梦能够预示未来。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But today, with all the scientific knowledge that we have, I think it's much harder to believe in these sorts of things.","cn":"但如今，凭借我们所拥有的各种科学知识，我认为人们更难相信这类事情了。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: My grandmother is superstitious, and she thinks dreams can predict the future.","cn":"W: 我祖母很迷信，她认为梦可以预示未来。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Once she dreamed that the flight she was due to take the following day crashed.","cn":"有一次，她梦见自己第二天要乘坐的航班坠毁了。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Can you guess what she did?","cn":"你猜她做了什么？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"She didn't take that flight.","cn":"她没有乘坐那趟航班，甚至第二天都懒得去机场。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"She didn't even bother to go to the airport the following day.","cn":"相反，她乘坐了同一航班，不过是在一周之后。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Instead, she took the same flight but a week later.","cn":"当然，一切都很顺利。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"And everything was fine, of course.","cn":"根本没有飞机坠毁。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"No plane ever crashed.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: How funny!","cn":"M: 真有意思！"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Did you know that flying is actually safer than any other mode of transport?","cn":"你知道乘飞机其实比其他任何交通方式都安全吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"It's been statistically proven.","cn":"这在统计数据上已经得到了证明。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"People can be so irrational sometimes.","cn":"人有时候真的会很不理性。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Yes, absolutely.","cn":"W: 是的，完全正确。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But even if we think they are ridiculous, emotions can be just as powerful as rational thinking.","cn":"不过，即使我们觉得这些想法很荒谬，情感也可以和理性思维一样强大。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Exactly.","cn":"M: 没错。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"People do all sorts of crazy things because of their irrational feelings.","cn":"人们会因为不理性的情感而做出各种疯狂的事情。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But in fact, some psychologists believe that our dreams are the result of our emotions and memories from that day.","cn":"但事实上，一些心理学家认为，我们的梦是那一天的情感和记忆所产生的结果。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"I think it was Sigmund Freud who said that children's dreams were usually simple representations of their wishes, things they wished would happen.","cn":"我记得是西格蒙德·弗洛伊德说过，儿童的梦通常是他们愿望的简单呈现，也就是他们希望发生的事情。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But in adults, dreams are much more complicated reflections of their more sophisticated sentiments.","cn":"但对成年人来说，梦则是他们更复杂、更成熟的情感的复杂反映。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Isn't it interesting how psychologists try to understand using the scientific method something as bizarre as dreams?","cn":"W: 心理学家试图用科学方法去理解像梦这样奇怪的事物，难道不是很有意思吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Psychology is like the rational study of irrational feelings.","cn":"心理学就像是对非理性情感进行的理性研究。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"While some scientists explore the surface of Antarctica, others are learning more about a giant body of water four kilometers beneath the ice pack.","cn":"一些科学家在探索南极洲的地表，另一些科学家则在进一步了解冰盖下方四千米处的一片巨大水体。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Scientists first discovered Lake Vostok in the 1970s by using radio waves that penetrate the ice.","cn":"20世纪70年代，科学家首次利用能够穿透冰层的无线电波发现了沃斯托克湖。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Since then, they have used sound waves and even satellites to map this massive body of water.","cn":"此后，他们又利用声波，甚至卫星，对这片巨大的水体进行了测绘。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"How does the water in Lake Vostok remain liquid beneath an ice sheet?","cn":"沃斯托克湖的水为何能在冰盖下保持液态？"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"\"The thick glacier above acts like an insulating blanket and keeps the water from freezing,\" says Martin Siegert, a glaciologist from the University of Wales.","cn":"“上方厚厚的冰川就像一条隔热毯，防止湖水结冰，”威尔士大学的冰川学家马丁·西格特说。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"In addition, geothermal heat from deep within the earth may warm the hidden lake.","cn":"此外，来自地球深处的地热也可能使这个隐秘的湖泊保持温暖。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"The scientists suspect that micro-organisms may be living in Lake Vostok, closed off from the outside world for more than 2 million years.","cn":"科学家怀疑，沃斯托克湖中可能存在微生物，而这个湖泊已与外界隔绝了超过200万年。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Anything found there will be totally alien to what's on the surface of the earth, says Siegert.","cn":"西格特说，在那里发现的任何东西都将与地球表面的事物完全不同。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Scientists are trying to find a way to drill into the ice and draw water samples without causing contamination.","cn":"科学家正在设法钻入冰层并抽取水样，同时避免造成污染。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Again, robots might be the solution.","cn":"机器人或许又能成为解决方案。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"If all goes as planned, a drill-shaped robot will melt through the surface ice.","cn":"如果一切按计划进行，一台钻头形状的机器人将融穿表层冰层。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"When it reaches the lake, it will release another robot that can swim in the lake, take pictures, and look for signs of life.","cn":"当它抵达湖泊时，会释放出另一台能够在湖中游动、拍摄照片并寻找生命迹象的机器人。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"The scientists hope their discoveries will shed light on life in outer space, which might exist in similar dark and airless conditions.","cn":"科学家希望他们的发现能够为外太空的生命提供线索，因为那里可能存在处于类似黑暗且无空气环境中的生命。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Recently, close-up pictures of Jupiter's moon, Europa, show signs of water beneath its icy surface.","cn":"最近，木星的卫星 Europa 的特写照片显示，其冰封表面下方可能有水。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Once tested in Antarctica, robots could be sent to Europa to search for life there too.","cn":"机器人一旦在南极洲完成测试，就可以被派往 Europa，在那里寻找生命。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The idea to study the American Indian tribe Tarahumaras came to James Copeland in 1984 when he discovered that very little research had been done on their language.","cn":"年，詹姆斯·科普兰发现关于美国印第安部落塔拉乌马拉人的语言几乎没有开展过研究，于是产生了研究这个部落的想法。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He contacted a tribe member through a social worker who worked with the tribesmen in Mexico.","cn":"他通过一名在墨西哥与部落成员一起工作的社会工作者联系上了一位部落成员。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"At first, the tribe member, named Gonzalez, was very reluctant to cooperate.","cn":"起初，这位名叫冈萨雷斯的部落成员非常不愿意合作。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He told Copeland that no amount of money could buy his language.","cn":"他告诉科普兰，再多的钱也买不到他的语言。但在科普兰向他解释了自己打算如何开展研究，以及这项研究将如何使塔拉乌马拉人受益之后，冈萨雷斯同意提供帮助。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"But after Copeland explained to him what he intended to do with his research and how it would benefit the Tarahumaras, Gonzalez agreed to help.","cn":"他带科普兰去了自己的村庄，并担任中间人。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He took Copeland to his village and served as an intermediary.","cn":"科普兰说：“多亏了他，塔拉乌马拉人才明白我们的使命是什么，并开始信任我们。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Copeland says, \"Thanks to him, the Tarahumaras understood what our mission was and started trusting us.\"","cn":"”"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Entering the world of the Tarahumaras has been a laborious project for Copeland.","cn":"对科普兰来说，进入塔拉乌马拉人的世界是一个艰苦的项目。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"To reach their homeland he must drive two and a half days from Houston, Texas.","cn":"为了到达他们的家园，他必须从得克萨斯州休斯敦驾车两天半。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He loads up his vehicle with goods that the tribesmen can't easily get, and gives the goods to them as a gesture of friendship.","cn":"他把部落成员不容易获得的物资装满车辆，并将这些物资送给他们，以示友好。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The Tarahumaras, who don't believe in accumulating wealth, take the food and share it among themselves.","cn":"塔拉乌马拉人不相信积累财富，他们收下食物，并在彼此之间分享。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"For Copeland, the experience has not only been academically satisfying, but also has enriched his life in several ways.","cn":"对科普兰来说，这段经历不仅在学术上令人满足，也在多个方面丰富了他的生活。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"\"I see people rejecting technology and living a very hard, traditional life, which offers me another notion about the meaning of progress in the western tradition,\" he says.","cn":"他说：“我看到人们拒绝技术，过着非常艰苦的传统生活，这让我对西方传统中进步的含义有了另一种认识。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"\"I experience the simplicity of living in nature that I would otherwise only be able to read about.","cn":"我体验到了融入自然的简朴生活，否则我只能通过阅读来了解这种生活。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I see a lot of beauty in their sense of sharing and concern for each other.\"","cn":"我从他们分享和彼此关怀的观念中看到了许多美好。”"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"What is a radical?","cn":"什么是激进派？"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It seems today that people are terrified of the term, particularly of having the label attached to them.","cn":"如今，人们似乎对“激进”这个词感到恐惧，尤其害怕被贴上这样的标签。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Accusing individuals or groups of being radical often serves to silence them into submission, thereby maintaining the existing state of affairs, and, more important, preserving the power of a select minority who are mostly wealthy white males in western society.","cn":"指责个人或群体激进，往往是为了迫使他们沉默并顺从，从而维护现状，更重要的是，维护西方社会中一个少数群体的权力，而这个群体主要由富有的白人男性组成。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Feminism is a perfect example of this phenomenon.","cn":"女权主义就是这一现象的一个典型例子。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The women's movement has been plagued by stereotypes, misrepresentations by the media, and accusations of man-hating and radicalism, when the basic foundation of feminism is simply that women deserve equal rights in all facets of life.","cn":"妇女运动一直饱受刻板印象、媒体的歪曲报道以及仇视男性和激进主义等指责的困扰，而女权主义的基本立场其实很简单：女性在生活的各个方面都应享有平等权利。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"When faced with the threat of being labelled radical, women back down from their worthy calls and consequently participate in their own oppression.","cn":"当面临被贴上激进标签的威胁时，女性会放弃自己正当的诉求，因而参与到对自身的压迫之中。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It has gotten to the point that many women are afraid to call themselves feminists because of the stigma attached to the word.","cn":"事情已经发展到这样的地步：许多女性因为“女权主义者”一词所带的污名，而不敢称自己为女权主义者。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"If people refuse to be controlled and intimidated by stigmas, the stigmas lose all their power.","cn":"如果人们拒绝受污名的控制和恐吓，污名就会失去全部力量。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Without fear on which they feed, such stigmas can only die.","cn":"没有恐惧作为滋养，这样的污名只能消亡。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"To me, a radical is simply someone who rebels against the norm or advocates a change in the existing state of affairs.","cn":"在我看来，激进派不过是反抗常规或主张改变现状的人。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"On close inspection, it becomes clear that the norm is constantly evolving and therefore is not a constant entity.","cn":"仔细考察便会发现，常规一直在不断演变，因此并不是一个恒定不变的事物。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"So why then is deviation from the present situation such a threat when the state of affairs itself is unstable and subject to relentless transformation?","cn":"那么，既然现状本身不稳定且不断发生变化，偏离当前状况为何会构成如此大的威胁呢？"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It all goes back to maintaining the power of those who have it and preventing the right of those who don't.","cn":"这一切都归结于维护掌权者的权力，以及阻止无权者获得权利。事实上，当我们从历史背景来看“激进”一词时，几乎每一位如今被我们视为英雄的人物，在其所处的时代都曾被认为是激进派。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"In fact, when we look at the word \"radical\" in a historical context, nearly every figure we now hold up as a hero was considered a radical in his or her time.","cn":"激进派是推动变革的人。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Radicals are people who effect change.","cn":"他们是历史书写其事迹的人。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They are the people about whom history is written.","cn":"废奴主义者是激进派；民权活动家是激进派；"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Abolitionists were radicals; civil rights activists were radicals; even the founders of our country in their fight to win independence from England were radicals.","cn":"甚至我们国家的创建者们在争取脱离英国、赢得独立的斗争中也是激进派。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Their presence in history has changed the way our society functions, mainly by shifting the balance of power that previously existed.","cn":"他们在历史上的存在改变了我们社会的运行方式，主要是改变了原有的权力平衡。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Of course, there are some radicals who've made a negative impact on humanity, but undeniably, there would simply be no progress without radicals.","cn":"当然，也有一些激进派对人类产生了负面影响，但不可否认，如果没有激进派，就根本不会有进步。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"That being said, next time someone calls me a radical, I will accept that label with pride.","cn":"话虽如此，下一次有人称我为激进派时，我会自豪地接受这个标签。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"We are very susceptible to the influence of the people around us.","cn":"我们非常容易受到周围人的影响。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"For instance, you may have known somebody who has gone overseas for a year or so and has returned with an accent, perhaps.","cn":"例如，你可能认识这样一个人：他出国待了一年左右，回来时或许已经带上了口音。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"We become part of our immediate environment.","cn":"我们会成为身边环境的一部分。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"None of us are immune to the influences of our own world, and let us not kid ourselves that we are untouched by the things and the people in our life.","cn":"没有人能够不受自己所处世界的影响，所以不要自欺欺人，以为我们不会受到生活中的事物和人的影响。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Fred goes off to his new job at a factory.","cn":"弗雷德去一家工厂开始了新工作。弗雷德休息十分钟喝咖啡，但其他工人却休息半个小时。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Fred takes his 10-minute coffee break, but the other workers take half an hour.","cn":"弗雷德说：“你们这是怎么回事？"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Fred says, \"What's the matter with you guys?\" Two weeks later, Fred is taking 20-minute breaks.","cn":"”两周后，弗雷德开始休息二十分钟。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"A month later, Fred takes his half hour.","cn":"一个月后，弗雷德也休息半个小时。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Fred is saying, \"If you can't beat them, join them.","cn":"弗雷德说：“既然无法击败他们，那就加入他们。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Why should I work any harder than the next guy?\"","cn":"凭什么我要比别人更卖力地工作？”"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The fascinating thing about being human is that generally we are unaware that there are changes taking place in our mentality.","cn":"人类最令人着迷的一点在于，通常我们并没有意识到自己的心态正在发生变化。这就像在新鲜空气中待了几个星期后重新回到城市的烟雾中，只有在那时我们才会意识到，自己已经习惯了那些难闻的气味。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"It is like returning to the city smog after some weeks in the fresh air—only then do we realize that we have become accustomed to the nasty smells.","cn":"和爱挑剔的人相处，我们就会学会批评；"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Mix with critical people and we learn to criticize; mix with happy people and we learn about happiness.","cn":"和快乐的人相处，我们就会学会了解幸福。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"What this means is that we need to decide what we want from life and then choose our company accordingly.","cn":"这意味着，我们需要决定自己想从生活中得到什么，然后据此选择与自己相伴的人。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"You may well say, \"That is going to take some effort.","cn":"你很可能会说：“那需要付出一些努力。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"It may not be comfortable.","cn":"这样做可能会让人感到不自在。我可能会得罪现在身边的一些人。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"I may offend some of my present company.\" Right, but it is your life.","cn":"”没错，但这是你的人生。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Fred may say, \"I'm always broke, frequently depressed.","cn":"弗雷德可能会说：“我总是身无分文，经常感到沮丧。我一事无成，也从来没有做过什么令人兴奋的事。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"I'm going nowhere and I never do anything exciting.\" Then we discover that Fred's best friends are always broke, frequently depressed, going nowhere and wishing that life was more exciting.","cn":"”然后我们发现，弗雷德最要好的朋友也总是身无分文，经常感到沮丧，一事无成，并且总希望生活能更加精彩。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"This is not a coincidence.","cn":"这并非巧合。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Nor is it our business to stand in judgment of Fred.","cn":"我们也没有资格对弗雷德妄加评判。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"However, if Fred ever wants to improve his quality of life, the first thing he'll need to do is recognize what has been going on all these years.","cn":"然而，如果弗雷德有一天想要改善自己的生活质量，他首先需要做的，就是认识到这些年来一直发生着什么。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"It's no surprise that doctors as a profession suffer a lot of ill health because they spend their lives around sick people.","cn":"医生这个职业的人健康状况普遍较差，并不令人意外，因为他们一生都在与病人相处。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Psychiatrists have a higher incidence of suicide in their profession for related reasons.","cn":"精神科医生的职业自杀率更高，原因与此相关。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Traditionally, 9 out of 10 children whose parents smoke, smoke themselves.","cn":"传统上，父母吸烟的孩子中，十个有九个也会吸烟。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Obesity is in part an environmental problem.","cn":"肥胖在一定程度上是一个环境问题。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Successful people have successful friends.","cn":"成功人士身边也都是成功人士。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"And so the story goes on.","cn":"这样的例子还有很多。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Virtually every American can recognize a dollar bill at a mere glance.","cn":"几乎每个美国人只需一眼就能认出一张美元钞票。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Many can identify it by its sound or texture.","cn":"许多人甚至能凭声音或质感辨认出它。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"But few people indeed can accurately describe the world's most powerful, important currency.","cn":"然而，真正能够准确描述这种世界上最强大、最重要的货币的人确实寥寥无几。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The American dollar bill is colored with black ink on one side and green on the other; the exact composition of the paper and ink is a closely guarded government secret.","cn":"美元钞票一面用黑色油墨印刷，另一面用绿色油墨印刷；"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Despite its weighty importance, the dollar bill actually weighs little.","cn":"纸张和油墨的确切成分是政府严密保守的秘密。尽管美元钞票意义重大，但它实际上很轻。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"It requires nearly 500 bills to tip the scales at a pound.","cn":"将近500张钞票才有一磅重。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Not only is the dollar bill lightweight, but it also has a brief life span.","cn":"美元钞票不仅重量轻，而且使用寿命也很短。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Few dollar bills survive longer than 18 months.","cn":"很少有美元钞票能保存超过18个月。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The word \"dollar\" is taken from the German word \"thaler,\" the name for the world's most important currency in the 16th century.","cn":"“dollar”一词源自德语单词“thaler”，后者是16世纪世界上最重要的货币的名称。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The thaler was a silver coin first minted in 1518 under the reign of Charles V, Emperor of Germany.","cn":"塔勒是一种银币，于1518年在德国皇帝查理五世统治时期首次铸造。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The concept of paper money is a relatively recent innovation in the history of American currency.","cn":"纸币的概念在美国货币史上是一项相对较新的创新。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"When the Constitution was signed, people had little regard for paper money because of its steadily decreasing value during the colonial era.","cn":"宪法签署时，人们对纸币并不看重，因为纸币在殖民时期的价值一直在下降。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Because of this lack of faith, the new American government minted only coins for common currency.","cn":"由于缺乏信任，新成立的美国政府只铸造硬币作为通用货币。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Interest-bearing bank notes were issued at the same time, but their purpose was limited to providing money for urgent government crises, such as American involvement in the War of 1812.","cn":"与此同时，政府也发行了计息的银行券，但其用途仅限于为紧急的政府危机提供资金，例如美国参与1812年战争。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The first noninterest-bearing paper currency was authorized by Congress in 1862, at the height of the Civil War.","cn":"年内战最激烈的时期，国会批准发行了第一种不计息的纸币。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"At this point, citizens' old fears of devalued paper currency had calmed, and the dollar bill was born.","cn":"此时，公民对于纸币贬值的旧有担忧已经平息，美元钞票由此诞生。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The new green colored paper money quickly earned the nickname \"greenback.\"","cn":"这种新发行的绿色纸币很快获得了“绿背钞”的绰号。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Today, the American dollar bill is a product of the Federal Reserve, and is issued from the twelve Federal Reserve banks around the United States.","cn":"如今，美元钞票由联邦储备系统发行，并由遍布美国的12家联邦储备银行发行。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The government keeps a steady supply of approximately two billion bills in circulation at all times.","cn":"政府始终维持着大约20亿张钞票的流通量。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Controversy continues to surround the true value of the dollar bill.","cn":"关于美元钞票实际价值的争议一直存在。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"American history has seen generations of politicians argue in favor of a gold standard for American currency.","cn":"美国历史上，一代又一代的政治家都曾主张美国货币实行金本位制。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"However, for the present, the American dollar bill holds the value that is printed on it, and little more.","cn":"然而，就目前而言，美元钞票的价值就是印在上面的面值，仅此而已。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The only other guarantee on the bill is a Federal Reserve pledge as a confirmation in the form of government securities.","cn":"钞票上的唯一其他保障，是联邦储备系统以政府证券形式作出的保证，作为确认。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What happens during deep sleep according to the lecture?","options":["The brain deletes useless information","The brain moves patterns into long term memory","The brain stops working completely","The brain produces new words"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 During deep sleep, the brain replays these patterns and moves them into long term memory。"},{"q":"In the classic experiment, how much more did the sleeping students recall?","options":["Four percent","Fourteen percent","Forty percent","Four hundred words"],"answer":2,"explain":"原文说 recalled forty percent more words，多记住了百分之四十。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about catching up at the weekend?","options":["It fully repairs a week of short nights","It does not repair a week of short nights","It is better than regular sleep","It permanently harms memory"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 one long lie in does not repair a week of short nights，周末补觉弥补不了一周的睡眠不足。"}],"cloze":[{"text":"During deep sleep, the brain ______ these patterns and moves them into long term memory.","answers":["replays"],"hint":"重放、回放"},{"text":"Lack of sleep does more than ______ memory.","answers":["weaken"],"hint":"削弱"},{"text":"Keep a regular ______, and treat sleep as part of study.","answers":["bedtime"],"hint":"睡觉时间"}]},{"id":"cet4-2020-07-1","level":"CET4","exam":"2020_07_1","year":2020,"month":7,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2020年7月 四级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2020年7月 CET-4 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet4-2020-07-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Good morning. In today's headlines, Scotland's transport minister has warned of potentially extreme weather conditions as heavy snow is forecast across the country later this week. Orange warnings are in force for many areas for Wednesday and Thursday. The transport minister advised people in parts of Scotland covered by the orange alert to avoid travel on Wednesday. This is what he said to us: \"The orange warning may be raised to red in some areas. That is a warning for snow that has never been seen since the modern system came into place in Scotland.\" The orange warning has been extended until 6 p.m. on Thursday. Trains, planes and ferries are also likely to be affected, with a wind chill that could see parts of Britain feeling as cold as minus 15 degrees Celsius. The head of road policing said, \"I would urge drivers to take extra care on the roads for their journeys. Drivers should make sure they're prepared for their journey with warm clothing, food and drink, sufficient fuel and a charged mobile phone. There could be significant traffic delays, so please start to plan your journey now and consider if you really need to travel when conditions are this poor.\"","cn":"早上好。今日头条，苏格兰交通部长警告称，本周晚些时候全国范围内预报有大雪，可能出现极端天气状况。周三和周四许多地区发布了橙色预警。交通部长建议橙色预警覆盖的苏格兰部分地区的人们周三避免出行。他对我们说：\"橙色预警可能在某些地区升级为红色预警。这是自苏格兰现代预警系统启用以来从未见过的降雪预警。\"橙色预警已延长至周四下午6点。火车、飞机和渡轮也可能受到影响，风寒效应可能使英国部分地区体感温度低至零下15摄氏度。道路警务负责人表示：\"我强烈敦促驾驶员在行驶途中格外小心。驾驶员应确保为行程做好准备，携带保暖衣物、食物和饮料、充足的燃料以及充满电的手机。可能会出现严重的交通延误，因此请现在就开始规划您的行程,并考虑在这种恶劣条件下是否真的需要出行。\""},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Romania's wetlands are coming back to life thanks to help from local communities, the World Wildlife Fund, and funding from the European Union.","cn":"在当地社区、世界自然基金会的帮助以及欧盟的资助下,罗马尼亚的湿地正在恢复生机。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Roughly 2,224 acres of the picturesque Danube Delta—home to 300 species of birds—have been filled with wildlife.","cn":"风景如画的多瑙河三角洲约2224英亩的土地——这里是300种鸟类的栖息地——已经充满了野生动物。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The land has been connected to the network of lakes and streams in the area.","cn":"这片土地已与该地区的湖泊和溪流网络连接起来。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"\"A lot of birds have migrated to the area, and one doesn't need to travel long hours anymore or go to other lakes to watch the birds,\" says Ion Meuta, Deputy Mayor of Mahmudia.","cn":"Mahmudia副市长Ion Meuta说:\"许多鸟类已经迁徙到这个地区,人们不再需要长途跋涉或去其他湖泊观鸟了。\""},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The area around Mahmudia, which is a UNESCO World Heritage site, is the third-most bio-diverse in the world, after Australia's Great Barrier Reef and the Galapagos Islands.","cn":"Mahmudia周边地区是联合国教科文组织世界遗产地,是世界上生物多样性第三丰富的地区,仅次于澳大利亚大堡礁和加拉帕戈斯群岛。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Groups used earth-moving equipment to restore the waterways.","cn":"各团体使用土方设备恢复了水道。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Government officials proposed to protect the area's endangered wild fish by issuing a fishing ban over the next decade.","cn":"政府官员提议在未来十年内实施捕鱼禁令,以保护该地区濒危的野生鱼类。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Scott Dunn recently awoke from a medically-induced sleep he'd been in after a car accident. He was heartbroken after realizing he'd missed his high school graduation. So his classmates decided to give him another chance. It was just a month ago that East Juniata High School seniors met in the school's auditorium for graduation. And last week, they did it again. Scott's car accident was on May 22nd, just three days before the ceremony. \"I remember waking up in the hospital and asking mom what date it was. She told me it was the 28th,\" he said. \"I looked at her and said 'I missed my graduation.'\" The school's principal Mr. Fausey called Scott's mom Karen and said that everybody wanted to do something special for him. Students wore their caps and gowns and sat in the front of the auditorium. Scott's parents, Karen and Scott Senior, sat front and center. After brief speeches, Scott's name was called, only Scott's name. He walked across the stage as the audience cheered. A graduation for one. \"I'm speechless,\" Scott said. \"I don't know how to even explain it. I'm speechless to know that so many people are behind me.\"","cn":"Scott Dunn最近从车祸后的医学诱导睡眠中醒来。当他意识到自己错过了高中毕业典礼时心碎不已。于是他的同学们决定再给他一次机会。就在一个月前，East Juniata高中的毕业班学生在学校礼堂参加了毕业典礼。上周，他们又举行了一次。Scott的车祸发生在5月22日，距离典礼仅三天。\"我记得在医院醒来时问妈妈是几号。她告诉我是28号，\"他说。\"我看着她说'我错过了毕业典礼。'\"学校校长Fausey先生打电话给Scott的妈妈Karen，说大家都想为他做点特别的事。学生们穿着学位服和方帽，坐在礼堂前排。Scott的父母Karen和Scott Senior坐在正中央。简短致辞后，Scott的名字被宣读，只有Scott的名字。他走过舞台，观众欢呼。一个人的毕业典礼。\"我无法用言语表达，\"Scott说。\"我不知道该如何解释。知道有这么多人支持我，我无法用言语表达。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: How do you like your new flexible working arrangement?","cn":"M: 你觉得新的弹性工作安排怎么样？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Do you enjoy working from home?","cn":"你喜欢在家工作吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Yes and no.","cn":"W: 有好有坏吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I find isolation challenging at times.","cn":"有时候我觉得太孤独了挺难受的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Apart from my mother, not too many people I know have time for phone chats during working hours.","cn":"除了我妈，我认识的人里在工作时间能打电话聊天的真不多。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I tried the library, but found I wasn't really keen on working there.","cn":"我试过去图书馆，但发现我其实不太喜欢在那儿工作。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: No, neither would I.","cn":"M: 是啊，我也不会。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I find the library a bit too quiet.","cn":"我觉得图书馆有点太安静了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'd lack inspiration or stimulation, which would be counterproductive to getting a lot of work done.","cn":"我会缺乏灵感或刺激，这反而不利于完成很多工作。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I find the same thing.","cn":"W: 我也有同感。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"So, lately I've been going out to cafes occasionally.","cn":"所以最近我偶尔会去咖啡馆。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I love the noise, the people, the busyness of the café, the sense of being out in the world.","cn":"我喜欢那里的声音、人群、咖啡馆的热闹劲儿，还有那种置身于世界中的感觉。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Coffee shops seem to have effectively become office spaces for so many people in this digital age, though I'm not sure how cafe owners feel about it—having so many people who go to their places to work rather than drink and eat.","cn":"M: 在这个数字时代，咖啡店似乎已经有效地成为很多人的办公空间了，不过我不确定咖啡店老板对此有何感想——有那么多人去他们那儿是为了工作而不是喝咖啡吃东西。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Yes, some people seem to spend a lot of time there and not order much.","cn":"W: 是啊，有些人似乎在那儿待很长时间却点不了多少东西。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The most annoying ones for café owners must surely be those usually only two of them who occupy a table for six with their laptops and paperwork.","cn":"对咖啡店老板来说最烦人的肯定是那些人，通常只有两个人，却带着笔记本电脑和文件占着六人桌。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: They should sit at a table for two, not the table for six.","cn":"M: 他们应该坐两人桌，而不是六人桌。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Some obviously stay so long.","cn":"有些人显然待得太久了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"They need to plug the laptops into a power outlet.","cn":"他们需要把笔记本电脑插到电源插座上。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I nearly tripped over someone's computer electrical lead the other day in my local café.","cn":"前几天我在附近的咖啡馆差点被某人的电脑电源线绊倒。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: It's a double-edged sword. No doubt about that for a café owner. While remote workers help to keep the cafe full in quiet times, they can take up the valuable table space in busy periods.","cn":"W: 这对咖啡店老板来说是把双刃剑，毫无疑问。虽然远程工作者有助于在清淡时段保持咖啡馆满座，但在高峰时段他们会占用宝贵的桌位。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I'm going to start looking for another job.","cn":"W: 我打算开始找另一份工作了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I can't see myself getting an opportunity to progress at my company anytime in the near future.","cn":"我看不到自己在公司近期内有任何晋升的机会。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And I really think my skills and abilities deserve a higher salary.","cn":"而且我真的觉得我的技能和能力应该得到更高的薪水。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: You're not going to quit, are you?","cn":"M: 你不会要辞职吧?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I'm thinking I might as well.","cn":"W: 我觉得我不妨辞职。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Then I can devote more time and energy to finding a better position at another company.","cn":"这样我就能投入更多时间和精力在另一家公司找到更好的职位。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: But you've been at your present company less than two years, haven't you? This will be the third time you've left a job in the last five years. If you do several jobs in a relatively short span of time, prospective employers might perceive that you lack loyalty. That could make them wary and reluctant to employ you.","cn":"M: 但你在现在的公司还不到两年,是吧?这将是你过去五年里第三次离职了。如果你在相对较短的时间内换了好几份工作,潜在雇主可能会认为你缺乏忠诚度。这可能会让他们有所顾虑,不愿意雇用你。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Unfortunately, loyalty doesn't pay.","cn":"W: 不幸的是,忠诚并不会带来回报。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Even if I get a promotion at my company, it's likely to be less sizable than if I were to get a job elsewhere.","cn":"即使我在公司得到晋升,涨幅也可能不如我去别的地方找工作来得大。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And even if I get a promotion, I'm not guaranteed to get a raise.","cn":"而且即使我得到晋升,也不能保证会加薪。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I had that experience at another company I worked at.","cn":"我在之前工作的另一家公司就有过这样的经历。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: They wanted you to take on more work and responsibility but for the same amount of money?","cn":"M: 他们想让你承担更多的工作和责任,但工资还是一样?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: More or less, yes.","cn":"W: 差不多就是这样,是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The way I see it, through having different jobs, I've gathered a lot of experience in different jobs and in different industries.","cn":"在我看来,通过从事不同的工作,我在不同的岗位和不同的行业积累了大量经验。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: But potential employers might worry that, that experience is not deep, or thorough enough.","cn":"M: 但潜在雇主可能会担心那些经验不够深入或不够彻底。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Perhaps, but I feel pretty confident that I can sell myself.","cn":"W: 也许吧,但我很有信心能够推销自己。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You know what they say, \"Fortune favors the brave.\"","cn":"你知道他们怎么说的,\"幸运眷顾勇敢者\"。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"There is a saying that goes something along the lines of \"You must love yourself first before you can love someone else.\" Similarly, I personally believe that you must be comfortable and happy in your own company before you can truly be yourself in the company of others. There is a massive difference between being lonely and being alone. Loneliness is a horrible feeling. However, you don't have to actually be alone to feel that way. Many times, I've felt lonely when surrounded by a big group of people. In contrast, being alone can actually be a blessing, particularly when you've actively chosen it. In my experience, being bored and alone is dangerous and can easily lead to the feeling of loneliness. The trick is to be active. Get outside, stretch your legs, do something cultural, buy yourself something tasty to eat or something pretty to wear. You don't have to take anyone else into consideration and can do whatever you please. Spending time alone also allows you to more efficiently take care of problems. And then, when it's time to be social and meet up with your friends, you will be fully there, because you won't have too much other stuff floating around in your mind. Having been alone for a bit, you will also appreciate your friends' company more, and chances are, your time spent together will be more worthwhile.","cn":"有句话是这样说的：\"你必须先爱自己，然后才能爱别人。\"同样，我个人认为，你必须先在独处时感到自在和快乐，然后才能在他人陪伴下真正做自己。孤独和独处之间有着巨大的差别。孤独是一种可怕的感觉。然而，你并不一定要真正独自一人才会有那种感觉。很多时候，当我被一大群人围绕时，我感到孤独。相比之下，独处实际上可以是一种福分,特别是当你主动选择它时。根据我的经验，无聊和独处是危险的，很容易导致孤独感。诀窍在于保持活跃。走出去，活动一下筋骨，做点有文化气息的事，给自己买点好吃的或漂亮的衣服穿。你不必考虑任何其他人，可以做任何你想做的事。独处的时间也能让你更高效地处理问题。然后，当需要社交并与朋友见面时，你会全身心投入，因为你不会有太多其他事情在脑海中盘旋。独处一段时间后，你也会更加珍惜朋友的陪伴，而且很有可能，你们在一起度过的时光会更有价值。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"When I turned 12, I worked summers at my father's small brick cleaning business.","cn":"当我12岁时，我在父亲的小型砖块清洁公司做暑期工。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"I remember the harsh acid smell of the cleaning solution and the scraping sound of stiff iron brushes against rough brick.","cn":"我记得清洁溶液刺鼻的酸味，以及硬铁刷刮擦粗糙砖块的声音。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It was tempting to hurry a job—just finish.","cn":"人们很容易想草草了事——赶紧完工就好。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But anybody who worked for Thomas Kahoon had to meet his standards, and that included me.","cn":"但任何为Thomas Kahoon工作的人都必须达到他的标准，包括我在内。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"If I messed up, he made me stay late until I got it right.","cn":"如果我搞砸了，他会让我加班到做对为止。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"My father wasn't being mean.","cn":"我父亲并非刻薄。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"He demanded the same of himself.","cn":"他对自己也有同样的要求。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Every brick he cleaned on a house stood out like a red jewel in a white setting.","cn":"他在房子上清洁的每一块砖都像白色背景中的红色宝石一样醒目。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It was his signature.","cn":"那是他的标志。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In 1970, when I was 20, I got married and moved out of my parents' modest place into a housing project.","cn":"1970年，我20岁时结了婚，从父母简朴的住处搬到了一个住房项目区。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Drugs and gang violence were just beginning to plague the projects.","cn":"毒品和帮派暴力刚开始困扰这些项目区。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Some of my friends went to jail.","cn":"我的一些朋友进了监狱。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Some were killed.","cn":"有些人被杀了。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"My wife Verllen was 18 and nobody gave our marriage a chance.","cn":"我妻子Verllen当时18岁，没人看好我们的婚姻。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But we believed in each other and our faith made us strong.","cn":"但我们彼此信任，我们的信念使我们坚强。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"When we married, I worked as a stock clerk at Southwest Super Foods.","cn":"结婚时，我在Southwest Super Foods做库存管理员。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It was hard, tedious work.","cn":"这是一份辛苦而乏味的工作。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Each Friday night a truck came, with cases of food that had to be unloaded, priced, and placed on shelves.","cn":"每个周五晚上都有一辆卡车运来成箱的食品，必须卸货、标价并摆上货架。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Most of the stock clerks tried to get Friday night off.","cn":"大多数库存管理员都试图在周五晚上请假。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But I was always ready to work.","cn":"但我总是随时准备工作。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"By Saturday morning, all the cans and jars in my aisle were replaced with the labels facing smartly out, like a line of soldiers on review.","cn":"到周六早上，我负责通道上的所有罐头和瓶子都摆放整齐，标签整齐地朝外，就像一排接受检阅的士兵。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"That was my signature.","cn":"那是我的标志。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"I took pride in the job nobody wanted.","cn":"我为这份没人想做的工作感到自豪。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Watching more than three hours of television a day doubles memory loss in older people, a new study of more than 3,000 adults suggests.","cn":"一项针对3000多名成年人的新研究表明，每天看电视超过三小时会使老年人的记忆力丧失加倍。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Scientists at University College London used memory and fluency tests on the same group of people six years apart.","cn":"伦敦大学学院的科学家们对同一组人进行了相隔六年的记忆力和语言流畅性测试。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They found that those who watched on average less than three hours' television a day showed a decline of around four to five percent, while those who tended to watch more than three hours a day declined by an average of eight to ten percent.","cn":"他们发现，平均每天看电视少于三小时的人记忆力下降了约百分之四到五，而那些每天看电视超过三小时的人平均下降了百分之八到十。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The research team say they believe the \"alert-but-passive\" nature of television watching may be creating stress on the mind which contributes to memory decline.","cn":"研究团队表示，他们认为看电视\"警觉但被动\"的特性可能会对大脑造成压力，从而导致记忆力下降。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Older people who watch more television are also less likely to undertake activities known to preserve mental functioning such as reading, or interactive screen-based pursuits such as using the Internet or playing video games.","cn":"看电视较多的老年人也不太可能从事已知能保持心智功能的活动，如阅读，或基于屏幕的互动活动，如使用互联网或玩电子游戏。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The researchers say that television viewing may be a risk factor for Alzheimer's disease, but more research is needed to establish a link.","cn":"研究人员表示,看电视可能是阿尔茨海默病的一个风险因素，但需要更多研究来建立这种联系。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"While watching television may have educational benefits and relaxation benefits, the researchers advise that adults over the age of 50 should try and ensure that television viewing is balanced with other contrasting activities.","cn":"虽然看电视可能具有教育和放松的益处，但研究人员建议50岁以上的成年人应该努力确保看电视与其他对比性活动保持平衡。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"If you're concerned that the amount of television you're watching could have a negative impact on your health, you should limit the amount of TV you watch each day and undertake some healthy hobbies.","cn":"如果你担心观看电视的时间可能对健康产生负面影响，你应该限制每天看电视的时间并从事一些健康的爱好。"}]},{"id":"cet4-2020-12-1","level":"CET4","exam":"2020_12_1","year":2020,"month":12,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2020年12月 四级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2020年12月 CET-4 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet4-2020-12-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"A poisonous fish which has a sting strong enough to kill a human is invading the Mediterranean, warn scientists. The International Union for Conservation of Nature has raised concerns after the poisonous fish was spotted in the waters around Turkey, Cyprus, and the eastern Mediterranean. Native to the South Pacific and Indian Ocean, the potentially deadly fish has poisonous hooks and a painful sting capable of killing people. Although fatalities are rare, the stings can cause extreme pain and stop people breathing. The fish, often known as Devil Firefish, is a highly invasive species, and environmentalists fear its arrival could endanger other types of marine life. After being spotted in the Mediterranean, a marine scientist says, \"The fish is spreading, and that's a cause for concern.\"","cn":"科学家警告称，一种毒刺强度足以致人死亡的有毒鱼类正在入侵地中海。国际自然保护联盟在土耳其、塞浦路斯和地中海东部水域发现这种有毒鱼类后表达了担忧。这种鱼原产于南太平洋和印度洋,具有潜在致命性,长有毒钩,其painful刺伤能够致人死亡。虽然死亡案例罕见,但被刺伤可导致剧烈疼痛并使人呼吸停止。这种鱼通常被称为Devil Firefish,是一种高度入侵性物种,环保人士担心其到来可能危及其他海洋生物。一位海洋科学家在地中海发现该鱼后表示:'这种鱼正在扩散,这是一个令人担忧的原因。'"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Almost half the center of Paris will be accessible only by foot or bicycle this Sunday to mark World Car-Free Day.","cn":"本周日，巴黎市中心近一半的区域将仅允许步行或骑自行车通行，以纪念世界无车日。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"This is in response to rising air pollution that made Paris the most polluted city in the world for a brief time.","cn":"这是对日益严重的空气污染的回应，空气污染曾一度使巴黎成为世界上污染最严重的城市。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Mayor Anne Hidalgo promoted the first World Car-Free Day last year.","cn":"市长Anne Hidalgo在去年推动了首个世界无车日。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Hidalgo also has supported a \"Paris Breathes\" day.","cn":"Hidalgo还支持\"巴黎呼吸\"日。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"On the first Sunday of every month, Paris clears traffic from eight lanes of the main road.","cn":"每月的第一个周日,巴黎会清空主干道八条车道的交通。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"About 400 miles of streets will be closed to cars.","cn":"约400英里的街道将禁止汽车通行。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"It is expected to bring significant reduction in pollution levels.","cn":"预计这将显著降低污染水平。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Last year's car-free day showed a 40 percent drop in pollution levels in some parts of the city, according to an independent air pollution monitor, reports The Guardian—and sound levels dropped by 50 percent in the city's center.","cn":"据《卫报》报道，根据一家独立空气污染监测机构的数据，去年的无车日使该市部分地区的污染水平下降了40%，市中心的噪音水平下降了50%。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"A Philippine fisherman was feeling down on his luck when a house fire forced him to clear out his possessions and change locations. Then a good luck charm that he had kept under his bed changed his life. The unidentified man had fished out a giant pearl from the ocean when his anchor got stuck on the rock while sailing off the coastal island in the Philippines ten years ago. When he was forced to sell it, the shocked tourist agent at Puerto Princesa told him that the 77-pound giant pearl that he'd kept hidden in his run-down wooden house was the biggest pearl in the world, which was valued at 76 million pounds. The pearl of Allah, which is currently on display in a New York museum only weighs 14 pounds. That is 5 times smaller than the pearl that the fisherman just handed in. The monstrous pearl measured at one foot wide and 2.2 feet long is going to be verified by local experts and international authorities before hopefully going on display to attract more tourists in the little town.","cn":"一名菲律宾渔民正感到时运不济，一场房屋火灾迫使他清理自己的财物并搬迁。然后，他一直放在床底下的一个幸运符改变了他的人生。十年前，这名身份不明的男子在菲律宾沿海岛屿附近航行时，锚卡在了岩石上，他从海里捞出了一颗巨型珍珠。当他被迫出售它时，Puerto Princesa的旅游代理震惊地告诉他，他藏在破旧木屋里的这颗重77磅的巨型珍珠是世界上最大的珍珠，价值7600万英镑。目前在纽约一家博物馆展出的Allah之珠仅重14磅，比这名渔民刚刚上交的珍珠小5倍。这颗巨大的珍珠宽1英尺、长2.2英尺，将由当地专家和国际权威机构进行验证，然后有望在这个小镇展出以吸引更多游客。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Mr. Smith, it's a pleasure meeting you.","cn":"W: Smith先生，很高兴见到您。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Nice to meet you, too.","cn":"M: 我也很高兴见到你。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What can I do for you?","cn":"有什么我能帮你的吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well, I'm here to show you what our firm can do for you.","cn":"W: 嗯，我来这儿是想向您展示我们公司能为您做些什么。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Astra Consultants has branches in over 50 countries, offering different business services.","cn":"Astra咨询公司在50多个国家设有分支机构，提供各种商业服务。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We are a global company with 75 years of history, and our clients include some of the world's largest companies.","cn":"我们是一家拥有75年历史的全球性公司，我们的客户包括一些世界上最大的公司。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Thank you, Mrs. Houston.","cn":"M: 谢谢你，Houston女士。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I know Astra Consultants is a famous company.","cn":"我知道Astra咨询公司是一家知名公司。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But you said you would show me what you could do for me.","cn":"但你说你要向我展示你们能为我做什么。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Well, what exactly can your firm do for my company?","cn":"那么，你们公司具体能为我的公司做些什么呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: We advise businesses on all matters, from market analysis to legal issues, anything a business like yours could need.","cn":"W: 我们为企业提供各方面的建议，从市场分析到法律问题，任何像您这样的企业可能需要的服务。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Our firm offers expert advice.","cn":"我们公司提供专业建议。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Could I ask you, Mr. Smith, to tell me a little about your company and the challenges you face?","cn":"我能请您，Smith先生，跟我讲一讲您的公司以及您面临的挑战吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"That way I could better respond as to how we can help you.","cn":"这样我就能更好地回应我们如何能帮助您。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Okay, sure.","cn":"M: 好的，当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This is a family business started by my grandfather in 1950.","cn":"这是我祖父在1950年创办的家族企业。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We employ just over 100 people.","cn":"我们雇佣了100多名员工。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We manufacture and export stone for buildings and other constructions.","cn":"我们制造和出口用于建筑和其他建设的石材。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Our clients usually want a special kind of stone cut in a special design.","cn":"我们的客户通常需要按特殊设计切割的特殊石材。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And that's what we do in our factory.","cn":"这就是我们在工厂里做的事。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Our main challenge is that our national currency is rising, and we're losing competitive advantage to stone producers in India.","cn":"我们面临的主要挑战是我们国家的货币在升值，我们正在失去相对于印度石材生产商的竞争优势。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I see.","cn":"W: 我明白了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"That's very interesting.","cn":"这很有意思。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I would suggest that you let us first conduct a financial analysis of your company, together with an analysis of your competitors in India.","cn":"我建议您让我们先对贵公司进行财务分析，同时分析您在印度的竞争对手。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"That way we could offer the best advice on different ways forward for you.","cn":"这样我们就能为您提供关于不同发展方向的最佳建议。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Wow, congratulations, Simon!","cn":"W: 哇，恭喜你，Simon！"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The place looks absolutely amazing!","cn":"这地方看起来太棒了！"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Really?","cn":"M: 真的吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You think so?","cn":"你真这么觉得？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Of course.","cn":"W: 当然了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I love it.","cn":"我很喜欢。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It looks like you had a professional interior designer.","cn":"看起来像是请了专业室内设计师一样。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But you didn't, did you?","cn":"但你没有吧，对吧？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: No. I did it all by myself with a little help from my brother Greg. He's actually in the construction business, which was really helpful.","cn":"M: 没有。我全是自己做的，我弟弟Greg帮了点忙。他其实是做建筑行业的，这真的帮了大忙。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I honestly am impressed.","cn":"W: 我真的很佩服。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I know I could probably repaint the walls in my house over a weekend or something, but not a full renovation.","cn":"我知道我可能可以在一个周末之类的时间把家里的墙重新刷一遍，但做不了全面翻修。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Where did you get your ideas?","cn":"你的想法是从哪儿来的？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I wouldn't know where to start.","cn":"我都不知道从哪儿开始。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, for a while now, I've been regularly buying home design magazines.","cn":"M: 嗯，有一段时间了，我一直定期买家居设计杂志。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Every now and then, I'd save a picture I liked.","cn":"时不时地，我会保存我喜欢的图片。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Believe it or not, I had a full notebook of magazine pages.","cn":"信不信由你，我有满满一个笔记本的杂志页。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Since my overall style was quite minimal, I thought and hoped a whole renovation wouldn't be too difficult.","cn":"因为我整体风格相当简约，我觉得也希望整体翻修不会太难。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And sure enough, with Greg's help, it was very achievable.","cn":"果然，有Greg的帮忙，这很容易实现。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Was it very expensive?","cn":"W: 花费很贵吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I've imagined a project like this could be.","cn":"我想象这样的项目可能会很贵。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Actually it was surprisingly affordable.","cn":"M: 实际上出乎意料地便宜。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I managed to sell a lot of my old furniture and put that extra money towards the new material.","cn":"我设法卖掉了很多旧家具，把那笔额外的钱用在新材料上。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Greg was also able to get some discount materials from a recent project he was working on as well.","cn":"Greg还能从他最近做的一个项目那里弄到一些打折的材料。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Great.","cn":"W: 太好了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"If you don't mind, I'd like to pick your brains a bit more.","cn":"如果你不介意的话，我想再向你请教一下。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Jonathan and I are thinking of renovating our sitting room, not the whole house, not yet anyway.","cn":"Jonathan和我正在考虑翻修我们的客厅，不是整个房子，至少现在还不是。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And we'd love to get some inspiration from your experience.","cn":"我们很想从你的经验中获得一些灵感。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Are you free to come over for a coffee early next week?","cn":"下周初你有空过来喝杯咖啡吗？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Removing foreign objects from ears and noses costs England almost three million pounds a year, a study suggests. Children were responsible for the vast majority of cases—95% of objects removed from noses and 85% from ears. Every year an average of 1,218 nose and 2,479 ear removals took place between 2010 and 2016. According to England's Hospital Episode Statistics, children aged one to four were the most likely to need help from doctors for a foreign object in their nose. Five- to nine-year-olds come to the hospital with something in their ears the most. Jewellery items accounted for up to 40% of cases in both the ears and noses of children. Paper and plastic toys were the items removed next most from noses. Cotton buds and pencils were also found in ears. According to the study, the occurrence of foreign objects in children is generally attributed to curiosity. Children have an impulse to explore their noses and ears. This resulted in the accidental entry of foreign objects. Any ear, nose and throat surgeon has many weird stories about wonderful objects found in the noses and ears of children and adults. Batteries can pose a particular danger. In all cases prevention is better than cure. This is why many toys contain warnings about small parts. Recognizing problems early and seeking medical attention is important.","cn":"一项研究表明，从耳朵和鼻子中取出异物每年给英格兰造成近三百万英镑的费用。儿童占据了绝大多数病例——从鼻子中取出异物的病例占95%，从耳朵中取出的占85%。2010年至2016年期间，平均每年进行1218例鼻腔异物取出和2479例耳部异物取出。根据英格兰医院就诊统计数据，一至四岁的儿童最有可能因鼻腔异物需要医生帮助。五至九岁的儿童因耳朵异物来医院就诊的最多。珠宝饰品占儿童耳朵和鼻子异物病例的40%。从鼻子中取出次多的物品是纸张和塑料玩具。棉签和铅笔也在耳朵中被发现。根据该研究，儿童出现异物的情况通常归因于好奇心。儿童有探索鼻子和耳朵的冲动，这导致了异物的意外进入。任何耳鼻喉外科医生都有许多关于在儿童和成人鼻子和耳朵中发现奇异物品的离奇故事。电池可能会带来特别的危险。在所有情况下，预防胜于治疗。这就是为什么许多玩具包含关于小部件的警告。及早发现问题并寻求医疗救助非常重要。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Good morning.","cn":"早上好。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Today, I would like to talk to you about my charity ReBicycle.","cn":"今天,我想和大家谈谈我的慈善组织ReBicycle。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But before that, let me introduce someone.","cn":"但在此之前,让我介绍一个人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"This is Leila Rahimi.","cn":"这位是Leila Rahimi。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"She was so scared when she first moved to New Zealand that she struggled to leave the house and would spend days working up the courage to walk to the supermarket for basic supplies.","cn":"她刚搬到新西兰时非常害怕,以至于她很难走出家门,需要花好几天时间鼓起勇气走到超市购买基本生活用品。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"After a few months of being quite down and unhappy, she was invited to join a local bike club.","cn":"在情绪低落和不快乐了几个月之后,她受邀加入了当地的一个自行车俱乐部。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"At this time, ReBicycle got involved and gave Leila a second-hand bicycle.","cn":"这时,ReBicycle介入并给了Leila一辆二手自行车。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Within weeks, her depression had begun to ease as she cycled.","cn":"几周之内,她的抑郁情绪开始缓解,因为她开始骑车了。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The bicycle totally changed her life, giving her hope and a true feeling of freedom.","cn":"自行车彻底改变了她的生活,给了她希望和真正的自由感。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"To date, ReBicycle has donated more than 200 bikes to those in need, and is now expanding bike-riding lessons as demand soars.","cn":"迄今为止,ReBicycle已向有需要的人捐赠了200多辆自行车,并且随着需求激增,现在正在扩大自行车骑行课程。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"With a bike, newcomers here can travel farther but for almost no cost.","cn":"有了自行车,这里的新移民可以走得更远,但几乎不需要花费任何成本。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The three hours a day, they used to spend walking to and from English language lessons, have been reduced to just one hour.","cn":"他们过去每天花三个小时步行往返英语课程,现在已经减少到只需一个小时。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Our bike-riding lessons are so successful that we are urgently looking for more volunteers.","cn":"我们的自行车骑行课程非常成功,我们迫切需要更多志愿者。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Learning to ride a bike is almost always more difficult for an adult, and this can take days and weeks, rather than hours.","cn":"对成年人来说,学习骑自行车几乎总是更困难,这可能需要几天甚至几周的时间,而不是几个小时。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"So if any of you have some free time during the weekend, please come join us at ReBicycle and make a difference in someone's life.","cn":"所以如果你们中有人在周末有空闲时间,请来加入我们ReBicycle,为他人的生活带来改变。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Thanks to the International Space Station, we know quite a bit about the effects of low gravity on the human body, but NASA scientists want to learn more.","cn":"多亏了国际空间站，我们对低重力环境对人体的影响有了相当多的了解，但NASA的科学家们想了解更多。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"To that end, they have been studying how other species deal with low gravity, specifically focusing on mice.","cn":"为此，他们一直在研究其他物种如何应对低重力环境，特别关注小鼠。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The results are both interesting and humorous.","cn":"研究结果既有趣又幽默。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The scientists first sent some mice in a specially designed cage to the International Space Station.","cn":"科学家们首先将一些小鼠装在specially designed的笼子里送往国际空间站。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The cage allowed them to study the behavior of the mice remotely from Earth via video.","cn":"这个笼子使他们能够通过视频从地球上远程研究小鼠的行为。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"As you'll notice in the video, the mice definitely seem uncomfortable at the beginning of the experiment.","cn":"正如你在视频中注意到的，小鼠在实验开始时显然感到不适。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They move around clumsily, drifting within the small confines of the cage, and do their best to figure out which way is up, but without success.","cn":"它们笨拙地移动，在笼子的狭小空间内漂浮，并尽最大努力搞清楚哪边是上，但没有成功。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"However, it's not long before the mice begin to catch on.","cn":"然而，没过多久小鼠就开始明白了。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They adapt remarkably well to their new environment and even use the lack of gravity to their advantage as they push themselves around the cage.","cn":"它们非常好地适应了新环境，甚至利用失重状态的优势在笼子里推动自己移动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"That's when things really get wild.","cn":"这时事情变得非常有趣。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The eleventh day of the experiment shows the mice are not just dealing with the gravity change but actually seem to be enjoying it.","cn":"实验的第十一天显示，小鼠不仅在应对重力变化，而且实际上似乎很享受它。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Several of the mice are observed running around the cage walls.","cn":"观察到几只小鼠在笼子壁上奔跑。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The scientists wanted to see whether the mice would continue doing the same kinds of activities they were observed doing on Earth.","cn":"科学家们想看看小鼠是否会继续做在地球上观察到的同类活动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The study showed that the mice kept much of their routines intact, including cleaning themselves and eating when hungry.","cn":"研究表明，小鼠基本保持了它们的日常习惯，包括清洁自己和饿了就吃东西。"}]},{"id":"cet4-2020-12-2","level":"CET4","exam":"2020_12_2","year":2020,"month":12,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2020年12月 四级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2020年12月 CET-4 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet4-2020-12-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"A waiter has returned a check worth nearly $424,000 to the retired social worker who lost it.","cn":"一名服务员将一张价值近42.4万美元的支票归还给了遗失它的退休社工。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The waiter found a bank envelope while cleaning off a table last Saturday at a restaurant.","cn":"上周六，这名服务员在餐厅清理桌子时发现了一个银行信封。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"He ran outside but the customer was gone.","cn":"他跑到外面，但顾客已经离开了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"He opened the envelope and got a shock.","cn":"他打开信封后大吃一惊。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"After an unsuccessful search, the restaurant's owner called the Daily News for help.","cn":"在搜寻未果后,餐厅老板致电《每日新闻》寻求帮助。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The \"relieved\" customer was reunited with her check on Wednesday.","cn":"周三,这位\"如释重负\"的顾客与她的支票重聚。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"It contained money from her apartment sale, already planned for a down payment on a new home.","cn":"支票里的钱来自她公寓的售款,原本计划用作新房的首付。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The customer did not tip the waiter after her meal.","cn":"这位顾客用餐后没有给服务员小费。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"She tried to give him money later on, but he graciously declined.","cn":"她后来试图给他钱,但他礼貌地拒绝了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The waiter, who's working his way through school, did accept the customer's apology and gratitude and said he was happy to have helped her.","cn":"这名正在半工半读的服务员接受了顾客的道歉和感谢,并表示很高兴能帮助到她。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The village of Maref in Alaska voted on Tuesday to move to the state's mainland. The move is due to global warming and rising sea levels. Most of the village's 169 registered voters took part in the town hall meeting. They decided in a vote of 89 to 78 to move from their land on Sarichef Island, near the Arctic Circle. Maref Council Secretary Donna Barr said the vote was largely symbolic. It will be costly financially to the community. \"About 15 years ago, they estimated the cost at $180 million. I would figure it's much higher now,\" Barr said. \"We don't see the move happening in our lifetime because of the funding.\" The village's roughly 650 residents have seen warming temperatures melt sea ice and permanently frozen land. This has resulted in houses falling into the water. At least 31 villages in Alaska face \"immediate threats\" due to climate change, the Government Accountability Office reported in 2009.","cn":"Alaska的Maref村在周二投票决定迁往该州大陆。此次搬迁是由于全球变暖和海平面上升。该村169名登记选民中的大多数参加了市政厅会议。他们以89票对78票的结果决定从北极圈附近Sarichef岛上的土地搬迁。Maref委员会秘书Donna Barr表示，这次投票在很大程度上具有象征意义。这将给社区带来巨大的财政负担。\"大约15年前,他们估计费用为1.8亿美元。我认为现在肯定要高得多，\"Barr说。\"由于资金问题，我们认为这次搬迁不会在我们有生之年发生。\"该村约650名居民目睹了气温升高导致海冰融化和永久冻土消融。这导致房屋掉入水中。美国政府问责办公室在2009年报告称，Alaska至少有31个村庄因气候变化面临\"直接威胁\"。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"A man in Halifax, Canada, wanted to find out if people were thankful for someone holding the door open for them.","cn":"加拿大Halifax的一名男子想要了解人们是否会对为他们开门的人表示感谢。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The social experiment showed that 99 out of 100 people expressed gratitude.","cn":"这项社会实验表明,100人中有99人表达了感激之情。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"\"I didn't think we were going to get 99.","cn":"\"我没想到会得到99个,'感恩职场'(Gratitude at Work)首席执行官Steve Foran说,'我不知道为什么,但我感到惊喜,因为人们的反应不仅仅是说声'谢谢',他们还和我们交谈。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"I don't know why, but I was pleasantly surprised because it went beyond just 'thank you.' People got into conversations with us,\" said Steve Foran, CEO of Gratitude at Work.","cn":"'他说:'研究表明,心怀感恩的人会带来美好的事物。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"\"What we know from research is that from grateful people come good things,\" he said.","cn":"'他说:'引发人们感恩之情的一个简单方法就是为他们开门,所以我们去了六个地方为人们开门。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"\"A simple way to induce gratitude in people is opening doors and so we went to six places and opened the doors for people.\" For the experiment, Foran's team went to a shopping center, a mall, two office buildings, and a coffee shop.","cn":"'在这项实验中,Foran的团队前往了一个购物中心、一个商场、两栋办公楼和一家咖啡店。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The door was held for 15 to 20 people at a time at each location.","cn":"在每个地点,他们每次为15到20人开门。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"\"We did have one that didn't say thank you.","cn":"'确实有一个人没有说谢谢。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"We're not here to judge them because on any given day, that could be me or you.","cn":"我们不是来评判他们的,因为在任何一天,那个人可能就是我或你。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"I suspect out of the 100 people, there were probably a bunch of them having a bad day, but grateful people make people grateful,\" said Foran.","cn":"我估计在这100人中,可能有一些人正在经历糟糕的一天,但心怀感恩的人会让其他人也心怀感恩,'Foran说。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Rays Solar. Lisa's speaking. How can I help?","cn":"W: Rays Solar,我是Lisa。有什么可以帮您?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Hi, my name is Winston.","cn":"M: 你好,我叫Winston。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I wish to enquire about solar panel installations.","cn":"我想咨询一下太阳能板安装的事。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Yes.","cn":"W: 好的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What would you like to know?","cn":"您想了解什么?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well. My neighbor installed panels on his roof about a year ago in order to power his hot water. He tells me it has saved him over $500 thus far. Does that sound about right to you?","cn":"M: 嗯,我邻居大概一年前在他屋顶上装了太阳能板,用来给热水供电。他告诉我到目前为止已经省了500多美元。这听起来对吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well. I'm not familiar with your neighbor or his particular setup, but that amount is definitely possible. I can tell you that the average four-bedroom house may typically have a roof with 50 square meters of surface area. Four panels on one side of that roof could save a family of four around $300 a year.","cn":"W: 嗯,我不了解您邻居的情况或他的具体配置,但这个金额是完全有可能的。我可以告诉您,一般四居室的房子屋顶表面积通常有50平方米。在屋顶一侧安装四块太阳能板,一个四口之家每年大约能省300美元。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: OK. That sounds about right then. My house is about the size you described, but my neighbor's is bigger. I'm not sure how many panels he has up there, but he does have a large family of six.","cn":"M: 好的,那听起来差不多。我家大概是您说的那个大小,但我邻居家更大。我不确定他屋顶上装了多少块板,但他家有六口人,是个大家庭。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Are you interested in installing some solar panels on your roof, sir?","cn":"W: 先生,您有兴趣在您的屋顶上安装太阳能板吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Yes, I'm considering it.","cn":"M: 是的,我在考虑。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: If you wish to come into our office, we could show you the different solutions we offer.","cn":"W: 如果您愿意来我们办公室,我们可以向您展示我们提供的不同方案。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: OK. I might do that. But just quickly, if you don't mind, could you tell me approximately how much a typical installation costs, like, say, four panels?","cn":"M: 好的,我可能会去。但如果您不介意的话,能不能快速告诉我大概的安装费用是多少,比如说四块板?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Prices do vary depending on different factors, but as a rough estimate, it's around $2,000.","cn":"W: 价格会因不同因素而有所变化,但粗略估计大约是2000美元。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But you know a typical household will make back that initial investment in about five years.","cn":"不过您知道,一般家庭大约五年就能收回最初的投资。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: OK. I see. Thank you.","cn":"M: 好的,明白了。谢谢。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Good afternoon.","cn":"M: 下午好。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Sorry to have kept you waiting.","cn":"抱歉让您久等了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"How can I help you?","cn":"有什么可以帮您的吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Oh, no problem.","cn":"W: 哦，没关系。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm interested in booking a holiday to Australia and wonder if you could tell me what deals you have.","cn":"我想预订去澳大利亚的假期，想了解一下你们有什么优惠套餐。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Sure.","cn":"M: 当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Are you only looking for flights or a package holiday with everything included?","cn":"您只是想订机票，还是想要包含所有服务的套餐假期？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: When you say \"everything,\" what do you mean?","cn":"W: 您说的\"所有服务\"是指什么？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, a package holiday would include your flights, hotels, meals, day trips to different places of interest and transport to and from the airport.","cn":"M: 嗯，套餐假期会包括您的机票、酒店、餐食、去各个景点的一日游以及机场往返接送。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yeah, that sounds pretty good.","cn":"W: 是的，听起来很不错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm going with my family, so it would be nice to have everything taken care of.","cn":"我要和家人一起去，所以如果一切都安排好了就太好了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So, what sort of deals do you have for package holidays then?","cn":"那么，套餐假期有什么优惠呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: All sorts, really.","cn":"M: 各种各样的都有。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"How long do you want to go for and what dates?","cn":"您想去多长时间，什么日期？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Two weeks around Christmas time would be great.","cn":"W: 圣诞节前后两周就很好。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Okay, let me check that for you.","cn":"M: 好的，让我给您查一下。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Here's one, 14 nights in southeastern Australia.","cn":"这有一个，在澳大利亚东南部住14晚。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Five nights in Sydney and five nights in Melbourne, and then for the other four nights you can choose from a list of trips to other places nearby.","cn":"在悉尼住5晚，在墨尔本住5晚，然后剩下的4晚您可以从附近其他地方的行程清单中选择。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You could visit Canberra, for example, or the Blue Mountains, or you could go for a drive down the Great Ocean Road.","cn":"比如您可以去堪培拉，或者蓝山，或者沿着大洋路自驾游。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Also, if you're interested in wine, you could go on a tour of the places where they grow grapes and make wine.","cn":"另外，如果您对葡萄酒感兴趣，还可以去参观葡萄种植和酿酒的地方。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That sounds great.","cn":"W: 听起来很棒。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's good we can choose some activities ourselves.","cn":"我们能自己选择一些活动真不错。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Tourists taking a holiday in the Indonesian island of Bali are facing a new $14-per-person tax when they arrive on the holiday island from next year. But this is a green tax, which Bali Governor Wayan Koster has been working on for months, and which is designed to help clean up the island's natural environment, and with good reason, too. Indonesia is drowning in plastics. Recycling is not one of the country's strong points. It's not uncommon to be offered many more plastic bags than one could ever need when visiting supermarkets and shopping malls. But, slowly, things are starting to change for the better. Back in 2016, the medium-sized city of Banjarmasin banned single-use plastic bags. The city of Bogor followed suit in 2018. A few months ago, Koster announced a plan that would not only ban single-use plastic bags from supermarkets and convenience stores, but plastic bags and straws across the island. The regulation will come into full effect next month. \"We received a fast and quick response from the Balinese people. Not only positive responses from the Balinese, we received good responses from the central government, other local governments and even from overseas.\" Koster told the Sydney Morning Herald this week during an interview. The governor is a determined environmentalist and he has more laws planned to protect the island's waterways, in particular, and to support the introduction of electric vehicles too.","cn":"明年起，前往印度尼西亚Bali岛度假的游客抵达这个度假岛屿时将面临每人14美元的新税费。但这是一项绿色税收，Bali省长Wayan Koster为此已经筹备了数月，旨在帮助清理该岛的自然环境，而且理由充分。印度尼西亚正被塑料淹没。回收利用并非该国的强项。在超市和购物中心购物时，被提供的塑料袋数量远超实际需要的情况并不罕见。但情况正在慢慢好转。早在2016年，中等规模城市Banjarmasin就禁止了一次性塑料袋。Bogor市于2018年效仿。几个月前,Koster宣布了一项计划,不仅要在超市和便利店禁止一次性塑料袋,还要在全岛范围内禁止塑料袋和吸管。该法规将于下月全面生效。\"我们收到了Bali人民快速而迅捷的回应。不仅有来自Bali人的积极反馈,我们还收到了中央政府、其他地方政府甚至海外的良好反馈。\"Koster本周在接受《悉尼先驱晨报》采访时表示。这位省长是一位坚定的环保主义者,他还计划制定更多法律来保护该岛的水域,特别是支持引入电动汽车。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"An endangered species of whale is experiencing a small-baby boom off the coast of America. The North Atlantic right whale is one of the rarest species of whale on the planet, numbering only about 411. But the Center for Coastal Studies said Friday that its aerial survey team spotted a mum with two babies in Cape Cod Bay a day earlier. That brings the number seen in nearby waters alone this year to three. That's big news because the whale population has been falling, and no baby whales were seen last year. In all, seven baby whales have been spotted so far this year. The whale population has become endangered due to commercial whaling activities in recent years. This is because they are sometimes hunted for their meat or their skin. Over-hunting could lead to the disappearance of the whale population, possibly causing major problems to the global food chain. The whales give birth off the Southeast Coast of America in the winter and travel to feeding grounds off the Northeast Coast in the early spring. The Northeast Coast is a critically important source of food. The animals often feed close to shore. This provides watchers on land with \"unbeatable views of one of the rarest of marine mammals.\" It's illegal to get within 1,500 feet of the animals without a federal research permit, so whale watchers are discouraged from attempting to get close to the whales.","cn":"一种濒危鲸鱼物种正在美国海岸附近经历一次小规模的婴儿潮。北大西洋露脊鲸是地球上最稀有的鲸鱼物种之一,数量仅约411头。但海岸研究中心周五表示,其空中调查团队前一天在科德角湾发现了一头母鲸和两头幼鲸。这使得今年仅在附近水域发现的幼鲸数量达到三头。这是个重大消息,因为鲸鱼数量一直在下降,而去年没有发现任何幼鲸。到目前为止,今年总共发现了七头幼鲸。近年来,由于商业捕鲸活动,鲸鱼数量已变得濒危。这是因为它们有时会因肉或皮被猎捕。过度捕猎可能导致鲸鱼种群消失,可能对全球食物链造成重大问题。这些鲸鱼在冬季于美国东南海岸产仔,并在早春前往东北海岸的觅食地。东北海岸是极其重要的食物来源。这些动物经常在近岸觅食。这为陆地上的观察者提供了'观赏这种最稀有海洋哺乳动物之一的绝佳视野'。未经联邦研究许可,靠近这些动物1500英尺以内是违法的,因此不鼓励观鲸者试图接近这些鲸鱼。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"An average person consumes 144 pints of milk a year, but 40% of that is poured onto cereal.","cn":"一个普通人每年消费144品脱牛奶，但其中40%被倒在麦片上。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"And 60% of those people are children.","cn":"而这些人中60%是儿童。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"But what was once advertised as nutritious is becoming unpopular.","cn":"但曾经被宣传为营养食品的牛奶正变得不受欢迎。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Americans drink 37% less milk than they did in the 1970s.","cn":"美国人喝的牛奶比20世纪70年代少了37%。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"And in the UK, dairy consumption overall has fallen by a third in the past 20 years.","cn":"而在英国，过去20年乳制品消费总体下降了三分之一。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Milk is increasingly being described in a negative light.","cn":"牛奶越来越多地被负面描述。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"A recent blog suggested maybe people are drinking less milk because it is poisonous to many of us.","cn":"最近一篇博客文章提出，也许人们喝更少牛奶是因为它对我们许多人来说有毒。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Lactose is the sugar found in milk and dairy products.","cn":"乳糖是牛奶和乳制品中发现的糖。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It needs a series of complex proteins to break it down.","cn":"它需要一系列复杂的蛋白质来分解它。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Without enough of these proteins, the lactose is broken down by bacteria in the human body.","cn":"如果没有足够的这些蛋白质，乳糖会被人体内的细菌分解。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This can cause physical pain and produce gas in the stomach.","cn":"这可能导致身体疼痛并在胃中产生气体。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"However, after we have finished breast or formula feeding, most of us don't continue producing the complex proteins in our body, which are necessary to break down the lactose.","cn":"然而，在我们断奶或停止配方奶喂养后，我们大多数人不再继续在体内产生分解乳糖所必需的复杂蛋白质。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Despite the problems in digesting milk, it does provide many benefits.","cn":"尽管消化牛奶存在问题，它确实提供许多益处。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Milk is nutritious.","cn":"牛奶有营养。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It contains vitamins A and D, as well as protein and isn't full of calories.","cn":"它含有维生素A和D，以及蛋白质，并且不含大量卡路里。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"You can test yourself by drinking a large glass of milk.","cn":"你可以通过喝一大杯牛奶来测试自己。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"If you get sick in your stomach within the next 24 hours, you are lacking in the proteins to digest milk.","cn":"如果你在接下来的24小时内胃部不适，你就缺乏消化牛奶的蛋白质。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2020-07-1","level":"CET6","exam":"2020_07_1","year":2020,"month":7,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2020年7月 六级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2020年7月 CET-6 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet6-2020-07-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Tonight, we have a very special guest.","cn":"M：今晚，我们请到了一位非常特别的嘉宾。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Mrs Anna Sanchez is a three-time Olympic champion and author of the new book To the Edge.","cn":"安娜·桑切斯夫人是三届奥运冠军，也是新书《逼近极限》的作者。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Mrs Sanchez, thank you for joining us.","cn":"桑切斯夫人，谢谢您参加我们的节目。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Thank you for having me.","cn":"W：谢谢您的邀请。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Let's start with your book.","cn":"M：我们先从您的书谈起吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What does the title To the Edge mean?","cn":"书名《逼近极限》是什么意思？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What are you referring to?","cn":"您指的是什么？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: The book is about how science and technology have helped push humans to the edge of their physical abilities.","cn":"W：这本书讲的是科学和技术如何帮助人类将身体能力推向极限。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I argue that in the past 20 years we've had the best athletes the world has ever seen.","cn":"我认为，在过去20年里，我们拥有了全世界有史以来最优秀的运动员。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: But is this a fair comparison?","cn":"M：但这种比较公平吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"How do you know how, say, a football player from 50 years ago would compare to one today?","cn":"比如说，您怎么知道50年前的足球运动员和今天的足球运动员相比会是什么情况？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well, you are right.","cn":"W：嗯，您说得对。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"That comparison would be perhaps impossible to make.","cn":"这种比较也许根本无法进行。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But the point is more about our knowledge today of human biochemistry, nutrition and mechanics.","cn":"但重点更多在于我们如今对人体生物化学、营养学和力学的了解。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I believe that while our bodies have not changed in thousands of years, what has changed is the scientific knowledge.","cn":"我认为，虽然我们的身体几千年来并没有改变，但发生变化的是科学知识。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This has allowed athletes to push the limits of what was previously thought possible.","cn":"这使运动员能够突破过去被认为不可能实现的极限。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: That's interesting.","cn":"M：这很有意思。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Please tell us more about these perceived limits.","cn":"请再多给我们讲讲这些所谓的极限吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: The world has seen sports records being broken that could only be broken with the aid of technology, whether this be the speed of a tennis serve or the fastest time in a 100-meter dash or 200-meter swimming race.","cn":"W：世界上已经出现了一些被打破的体育纪录，而这些纪录只有借助技术才能被打破，无论是网球发球的速度，还是100米短跑或200米游泳的最快成绩。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Is there any concern that technology is giving some athletes an unfair advantage over others?","cn":"M：有没有人担心技术会让一些运动员相较于其他人获得不公平的优势？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: That is an interesting question and one that has to be considered very carefully.","cn":"W：这是一个有意思的问题，也是必须非常慎重考虑的问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Skis, for example, went from being made of wood to a metal alloy, which allows for better control and faster speed.","cn":"比如，滑雪板从木制变成了金属合金制，这使运动员能够更好地控制滑雪板并获得更快的速度。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"There is no stopping technological progress.","cn":"技术进步是无法阻挡的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But, as I said, each situation should be considered carefully on a case-by-case basis.","cn":"但是，正如我所说，每种情况都应该具体问题具体分析。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I've worked in international trade all my life.","cn":"W: 我一辈子都在从事国际贸易。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"My father did so too before me.","cn":"在我之前我父亲也是做这行的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So I guess you could say it runs in the family.","cn":"所以我想可以说这是我们家族的传统吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: What products have you worked with?","cn":"M: 你都做过哪些产品？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: All sorts, really.","cn":"W: 真的什么都有。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I've imported textiles, machinery, toys, solar panels, all kinds of things over the years.","cn":"这些年来我进口过纺织品、机械、玩具、太阳能电池板，各种各样的东西。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Trends and demand come and go.","cn":"趋势和需求总是随时间变化。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So one needs to be very flexible to succeed in this industry.","cn":"在这个行业要取得成功，人必须非常灵活才行。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I see.","cn":"M: 我明白了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"What goods are you trading now?","cn":"那你现在在做哪些商品的贸易？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I now import furniture from China into Italy and foods from Italy into China.","cn":"W: 我现在把家具从中国进口到意大利，把食品从意大利进口到中国。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I even use the same container.","cn":"我甚至使用同一个集装箱。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's a very efficient way of conducting trade.","cn":"这是做贸易非常高效的一种方式。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: The same container?","cn":"M: 同一个集装箱？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You mean you own a 40-foot cargo container?","cn":"你是说你拥有一个40英尺的货运集装箱？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yeah. that's right.","cn":"W: 是的，没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I have a warehouse in Genova, Italy and another in Shanghai.","cn":"我在意大利热那亚有一个仓库，在上海也有一个。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I source mid-century modern furniture from different factories in China.","cn":"我从中国不同的工厂采购20世纪中期现代风格家具。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's very good value for money.","cn":"性价比非常高。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I collect it all in my warehouse and then dispatch it to my other warehouse in Italy.","cn":"我把它们全都在我的仓库集中起来，然后再发往我位于意大利的另一个仓库。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Over there I do the same, but with Italian foods instead of furniture, things like pasta, cheese, wine, chocolates.","cn":"在当地我也做同样的事，只不过换成了意大利食品而不是家具，像意大利面、奶酪、葡萄酒、巧克力之类的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And I send all that to my warehouse in China in the same freight container I use for the furniture.","cn":"然后我用装家具的同一个货运集装箱，把所有这些发往我在中国的仓库。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: So I presume you sell both lines of products wholesale in each respective country.","cn":"M: 这么说，我推测你在各自的国家都是批发销售这两条产品线了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Of course.","cn":"W: 当然了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I possess a network of clients and partners in both countries.","cn":"我在两个国家都有客户和合作伙伴网络。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"That's the main benefit of having done this for so long.","cn":"这就是干这行这么久的主要好处。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I've made great business contacts over time.","cn":"随着时间的推移，我积累了极好的商业人脉。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: How many times do you ship?","cn":"M: 你运货运多少次？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I did 12 shipments last year, 18 this year, and I hope to grow to around 25 next year.","cn":"W: 我去年运了12趟，今年18趟，我希望明年能增加到25趟左右。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"That's both ways, there and back again.","cn":"这是双向的，去一趟再回一趟。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Demand for authentic Italian food in China is growing rapidly.","cn":"中国对正宗意大利食品的需求正在快速增长。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And similarly, sales of affordable, yet stylish wooden furniture are also increasing in Italy.","cn":"同样地，在意大利，实惠又时尚的木质家具销量也在增加。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Furniture is marginally more profitable, mostly because it enjoys lower customs duties.","cn":"家具的利润要稍微高一点，主要是因为它享受更低的关税。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"\"Too many people view their jobs as a five-day prison from which they are paroled every Friday,\" says Joel Goodman, founder of the Humour Project, a humour consulting group in Saratoga Springs, New York. Humour unlocks the office prison because it lets adults bring some of their childlike spirit to the job.","cn":"“太多人把自己的工作看作一座为期五天的监狱，每周五才获准假释出来。”纽约州萨拉托加斯普林斯市 Humour Project（幽默项目）创始人乔尔·古德曼说。幽默能够打开办公室这座监狱，因为它让成年人得以把一些孩子般的天性带到工作中来。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"According to Howard Pollio, professor of psychology at the University of Tennessee, Knoxville, an office with humour breaks is an office with satisfied and productive employees.","cn":"据田纳西大学诺克斯维尔分校心理学教授霍华德·波利奥说，有幽默休息时间的办公室里，员工会更满意，工作效率也更高。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Pollio conducted a study that proved humour can help workers excel at routine production tasks.","cn":"波利奥进行了一项研究，证明幽默能够帮助员工出色地完成常规生产任务。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Employees perform better when they have fun.","cn":"当员工感到快乐时，他们的表现会更好。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"In large corporations with a hierarchy of power, there is often no outlet for stress. \"Every company needs underground ways of poking fun at the organization,\" says Lynn N. Mark, a speaker on workplace humour for St. Mary's Health Centre in St. Louis.","cn":"在拥有权力等级制度的大型企业中，压力往往没有宣泄的出口。“每家公司都需要一些地下方式来拿组织开玩笑，”圣路易斯 St. Mary's Health Centre（圣玛丽健康中心）职场幽默演讲人林恩·N·马克说。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Kodak's Rochester, New York branch discovered a way for its 20,000 employees to uncork their bottled-up resentments.","cn":"纽约州罗切斯特市的柯达分公司找到了一种方法，让其两万名员工发泄积压已久的怨气。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Their 1,000-square-foot Humour Room features a toy store.","cn":"他们那间面积达一千平方英尺的 Humour Room（幽默室）里设有一家玩具店。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Among the room's many stress-reducing gadgets, the main attraction is a boss doll with detachable arms and legs.","cn":"在房间里众多减压玩具中，最吸引人的是一个胳膊和腿都可以拆卸的老板玩偶。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Employees can take the doll apart as long as they put its arms and legs back in place.","cn":"员工可以把玩偶拆开，只要之后把它的胳膊和腿装回原位即可。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Sandy Cohen, owner of a graphic print production business, created the Quote Board to document the bizarre phrases people say when under strict deadlines. \"When you're under stress, you say stupid things,\" says Cohen. \"Now we just look at each other and say, that's one for the Quote Board.\"","cn":"平面印刷制作企业老板桑迪·科恩创设了 Quote Board，用来记录人们在严格的截止期限压力下说出的怪异话语。“人在压力之下会说些蠢话，”科恩说。“现在我们只要互相看一眼，说一句‘这句话得记到 Quote Board 上了’。”"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Public interest was aroused by the latest discovery of a changed gene in obese mice.","cn":"最新在肥胖小鼠身上发现变异基因一事引起了公众的兴趣。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The news was made known by Rockefeller University geneticist Jeffrey Friedman.","cn":"这一消息由洛克菲勒大学的遗传学家杰弗里·弗里德曼公布。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The researchers believe this gene influences development of a hormone that tells the organism how fat or full it is.","cn":"研究人员认为，该基因会影响一种能告知生物体其肥胖程度或饱腹状态的激素的生成。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Those with the changed gene may not sense when they have eaten enough or if they have sufficient fatty tissue, and thus can't tell when to stop eating.","cn":"携带该变异基因的个体可能无法感知自己何时已经吃饱，或者是否有足够的脂肪组织，因而无法判断何时停止进食。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The researchers also reported finding a gene nearly identical to the mouse obesity gene in humans. The operation of this gene in humans has not yet been demonstrated, however. Still, professionals like University of Vermont psychologist Esther Rothblum reacted enthusiastically: \"This research indicates that people really are born with a tendency to have a certain weight, just as they are to have a particular skin color or height.\"","cn":"研究人员还报告称，在人体内发现了与小鼠肥胖基因几乎完全相同的基因。然而，该基因在人体内的运行机制尚未得到证实。尽管如此，佛蒙特大学的心理学家埃丝特·罗斯布鲁姆等专业人士依然做出了热烈的反响：“这项研究表明，人们确实天生就具有保持某种体重的倾向，就像天生具有特定肤色或身高一样。”"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Actually, behavioral geneticists believe that less than half of the total weight variation is programmed in the genes, while height is almost entirely genetically determined.","cn":"实际上，行为遗传学家认为，总体重变化中只有不到一半是由基因决定的，而身高则几乎完全由基因决定。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Whatever role genes play, Americans are getting fatter.","cn":"无论基因扮演什么角色，美国人都在变得越来越胖。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"A survey by the Center for Disease Control found that obesity has increased greatly over the last 10 years.","cn":"疾病控制中心的一项调查发现，在过去10年中，肥胖率大幅上升。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Such rapid change underlines the role of environmental factors, like the abundance of rich foods, in Americans' overeating.","cn":"如此迅速的变化凸显了环境因素（例如丰富的高热量食物）在美国人过度进食中所起的作用。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The Center for Disease Control has also found that teens are far less physically active than they were even a decade ago.","cn":"疾病控制中心还发现，青少年目前的体育活动量远不及十年前。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Accepting that weight is predetermined can relieve guilt for overweight people.","cn":"接受体重是预先确定的观点可以减轻超重人群的罪恶感。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But people's belief that they cannot control their weight can itself contribute to obesity.","cn":"然而，人们认为自己无法控制体重的这一观念本身就会导致肥胖。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Qualities of a relationship, such as openness, compassion, and mental stimulation are of concern to most of us regardless of sex, but—judging from the questionnaire response—they are more important to women than to men.","cn":"关系中的一些品质，例如坦诚、同情心和精神上的相互启发，无论男女，大多数人都很看重；但从问卷的回答来看，女性比男性更为重视这些品质。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Asked to consider the ingredients of close friendship, women rated these qualities above all others.","cn":"当被要求考虑亲密友谊的构成要素时，女性给这些品质的评价高于其他所有品质。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Men assigned a lower priority to them in favor of similarity in interests, selected by 77% of men, and responsiveness in a crisis, chosen by 61% male respondents.","cn":"男性则将它们置于较低优先级，更看重兴趣相投（77%的男性选择了这一点）以及在危机时给予回应（61%的男性受访者选择了这一点）。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Mental stimulation, ranked third in popularity by men as well as women, was the only area of overlap.","cn":"精神上的相互启发在男性和女性中都颇受欢迎，排名第三，是双方唯一重合的方面。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Among men, only 28% named openness as an important quality; caring was picked by just 23%.","cn":"在男性中，只有28%的人认为坦诚是一项重要品质；选择关怀的仅有23%。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It is evident by their selections that when women speak of close friendships they are referring to emotional factors, while men emphasize the pleasure they find in a friend's company.","cn":"从她们的选择可以明显看出，女性谈到亲密友谊时，指的是情感因素；而男性则强调从朋友陪伴中获得的乐趣。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"That is, when a man speaks of \"a friend\" he is likely to be talking about someone he does things with—a teammate, a fellow hobbyist, a drinking buddy.","cn":"也就是说，当一个男人说“朋友”时，他很可能是在谈论一个和自己一起做事情的人——队友、共同从事某种爱好的人，或酒友。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"These activities are the fabric of the friendship; it is a \"doing\" relationship in which similarity in interests is the key bond.","cn":"这些活动构成了友谊的基础；这是一种“做事型”的关系，其中兴趣相投是维系关系的关键纽带。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This factor was a consideration of less than 11% of women.","cn":"只有不到11%的女性把这一因素视为考量。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Women opt for a warm, emotional atmosphere where communication flows freely; activity is mere background.","cn":"女性选择的是一种温暖而富有情感的氛围，在那里交流能够自由进行；活动本身只是背景。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Lastly, men, as we have seen, have serious questions about each other's loyalty. Perhaps this is why they placed such strong emphasis on responsiveness in a crisis—\"someone I can call on for help.\" Women, as their testimonies indicate, are generally more secure with each other and consequently are more likely to treat this issue lightly. In follow-up interviews this was confirmed numerous times as woman after woman indicated that \"being there when needed was taken for granted.\"","cn":"最后，正如我们所看到的，男性对彼此的忠诚抱有严重疑虑。或许这就是为什么他们如此强调在危机时给予回应——“一个我可以求助的人”。正如她们的陈述所表明的，女性彼此相处时通常更有安全感，因此更可能对此问题一带而过。在后续访谈中，这一点得到了多次证实：一个又一个女性表示，“需要时陪在身边”是理所当然的。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"As for the hazards of friendship, more than a few relationships have been shattered because of cutthroat competition and feelings of betrayal.","cn":"至于友谊中的风险，不少关系都因你死我活的竞争和被背叛的感受而破裂。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This applies to both men and women, but unequally.","cn":"这一点男女都适用，但程度并不相同。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"In comparison, nearly twice as many men complained about these issues as women.","cn":"相比之下，抱怨这些问题的男性几乎是女性的两倍。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Further, while competition and betrayal are the main thorns to female friendship, men are plagued in almost equal amounts by two additional issues: lack of frankness and a fear of appearing unmanly.","cn":"此外，尽管竞争和背叛是女性友谊中最主要的刺痛点，男性还几乎同等程度地受到另外两个问题的困扰：缺乏坦率，以及害怕显得不够男子气概。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Obviously, for a man, a good friendship is hard to find.","cn":"显然，对男人来说，一段美好的友谊很难寻得。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The partial skeletons of more than 20 dinosaurs and the scattered bones of about 300 more have been discovered in Utah and Colorado at what is now the Dinosaur National Monument.","cn":"在如今的恐龙国家纪念地，即犹他州和科罗拉多州交界一带，人们发现了20多具恐龙的部分骨骼以及约300具恐龙的零散骨骼。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Many of the best specimens may be seen today at museums of natural history in the larger cities of the United States and Canada.","cn":"如今，在美国和加拿大较大城市的自然历史博物馆里，可以看到许多保存最完好的标本。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This dinosaur pit is the largest and best preserved deposit of dinosaurs known today.","cn":"这处恐龙化石坑是迄今所知规模最大、保存最完好的恐龙沉积地。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Many people get the idea from the mass of bones in the pit wall that some disaster such as a volcanic explosion or a sudden flood killed a whole herd of dinosaurs in this area.","cn":"恐龙坑坑壁上大量的骨骼使许多人认为，某种灾难——例如火山爆发或突发洪水——在这一地区杀死了整群恐龙。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This could have happened but it probably did not.","cn":"这种情况本来可能发生过，但很可能并非如此。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The main reasons for thinking otherwise are the scattered bones and the thickness of the deposit.","cn":"之所以有理由作出不同的判断，主要是因为骨骼分布零散，而且沉积层很厚。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In other deposits where the animals were thought to have died together, the skeletons were usually complete and often all the bones were in their proper places.","cn":"在其他被认为是动物同时死亡形成的沉积地中，骨骼通常是完整的，而且所有骨头往往都处在各自应有的位置。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Rounded pieces of fossil bone have been found here.","cn":"这里曾发现过圆润的化石骨片。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"These fragments got their smooth round shape by rolling along the stream bottom.","cn":"这些碎片是在溪流底部滚动时形成光滑圆润的形状的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In a mass killing, the bones would have been left on the stream or lake bottom together at the same level.","cn":"如果是大量动物同时死亡，骨头就会一起留在溪流或湖泊底部的同一水平面上。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But in this deposit, the bones occur throughout a zone of sandstone about 12 feet thick.","cn":"但在这处沉积地中，骨头分布在一层约12英尺厚的砂岩带内。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The mixture of swamp dwellers and dry-land types also seems to indicate that the deposit is a mixture from different places.","cn":"沼泽栖息型动物和旱地型动物混杂在一起，这似乎也表明该沉积地是由来自不同地点的遗骸混合形成的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The pit area is a large dinosaur graveyard, not a place where they died.","cn":"这个坑区是一处大型恐龙墓地，而不是恐龙死亡的地方。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Most of the remains probably floated down an eastward flowing river until they were left on a shallow sandbar.","cn":"大多数遗骸很可能顺着一条向东流淌的河漂流而下，直到被冲到一处浅沙洲上。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Some of them may have come from far-away dry-land areas to the west.","cn":"有些遗骸可能来自西面遥远的旱地区域。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Perhaps they drowned trying to cross a small stream or were washed away during floods.","cn":"它们或许是在试图渡过一条小溪时溺水，也可能是在洪水中被冲走的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Some of the swamp dwellers may have got stuck in the very sandbar that became their grave; others may have floated for miles before being stranded.","cn":"一些沼泽栖息型动物可能陷在后来成为它们墓地的那片沙洲中；另一些则可能漂流了数英里，最后搁浅在那里。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Even today similar events take place.","cn":"即使在今天，类似的事情也会发生。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"When floods come in the spring, sheep, cattle and deer are often trapped by rising waters and often drown.","cn":"春季洪水来临时，绵羊、牛和鹿常常会被上涨的水流困住，并经常因此溺死。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Their dead bodies float downstream until the flood recedes and leaves them stranded on a bar or shore where they lie, half buried in the sand, until they decay.","cn":"它们的尸体顺流漂下，直到洪水退去，把它们留在沙洲或岸边搁浅；它们半埋在沙中，直到腐烂。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Early travelers on the Missouri river reported that shores and bars were often lined with the decaying bodies of buffalo that had died during spring floods.","cn":"早期在密苏里河上旅行的人报告说，河岸和沙洲上常常排列着在春季洪水中死亡的野牛腐烂尸体。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"I would like particularly to talk about the need to develop a new style of aging in our own society.","cn":"我尤其想谈谈在我们自己的社会中形成一种新的老年生活方式的必要性。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Young people in this country have been accused of not caring for their parents the way they would have in the old country.","cn":"这个国家的年轻人被指责没有像他们在故国时那样照料父母。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And this is true.","cn":"这确实如此。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But it is also true that old people have been influenced by an American ideal of independence and autonomy.","cn":"但同样确实的是，老年人也受到了美国式独立与自主理念的影响。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"So we live alone, perhaps on the verge of starvation, in time without friends, but we are independent.","cn":"因此，我们独自生活，也许处于饥饿的边缘，生活中没有朋友，但我们是独立的。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This standard American style has been forced on every ethnic group, although there are many groups for whom the ideal is not practical.","cn":"这种标准的美国式生活方式被强加给了每一个族群，尽管有许多族群并不适合这种理想。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It is a poor ideal and pursuing it does a great deal of harm.","cn":"这是一个糟糕的理想，追求它会造成极大的伤害。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This ideal of independence also contains a tremendous amount of unselfishness.","cn":"这种独立的理想还包含着极大程度的无私。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In talking to today's young mothers. I have asked them what kind of grandmothers they think they are going to be. I hear devoted, loving mothers say that when they are through raising their children, they have no intention of becoming grandmothers. They are astonished to hear that in most of the world throughout most of its history, families have been three- or four-generation families, living under the same roof.","cn":"我在与如今的年轻母亲交谈时，问过她们认为自己将会成为怎样的祖母。我听到一些全心投入、充满爱心的母亲说，等她们把孩子抚养成人后，她们根本不打算成为祖母。得知在世界上大多数地方、在其大部分历史时期，家庭都是三代或四代同堂、共同生活在一个屋檐下的家庭，她们感到十分惊讶。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"We have over-emphasized the small family unit—father, mother, small children.","cn":"我们过分强调了小家庭单位——父亲、母亲和年幼的孩子。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"We think it is wonderful if grandma and grandpa, if they're still alive, can live alone.","cn":"如果奶奶和爷爷还健在，并且能够独自生活，我们就认为这很了不起。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"We have reached the point where we think the only thing we can do for our children is to stay out of their way and the only thing we can do for our daughter-in-law is to see as little of her as possible.","cn":"我们已经到了这样一种地步：认为我们能为孩子做的唯一事情就是不妨碍他们，而我们能为儿媳做的唯一事情就是尽可能少见她。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Old people's nursing homes, even the best run, are filled with older people who believe the only thing they can do for their children is to look cheerful when they come to visit.","cn":"老年人的养老院，即使是管理得最好的养老院，也住满了这样一些老年人：他们认为自己能为子女做的唯一事情，就是在子女来探望时表现得兴高采烈。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"So in the end, older people have to devote all their energies to \"not being a burden\".","cn":"因此，到最后，老年人不得不把全部精力都用在“不成为负担”上。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"We are beginning to see what a tremendous price we've paid for our emphasis on independence and autonomy.","cn":"我们开始看到，过分强调独立与自主让我们付出了多么巨大的代价。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"We've isolated old people and we've cut off the children from their grandparents.","cn":"我们使老年人与世隔绝，也切断了孩子与祖父母之间的联系。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"One of the reasons we have as bad a generation gap today as we do is that grandparents have stepped out.","cn":"我们如今之所以存在如此严重的代沟，其中一个原因就是祖父母退出了生活。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Young people are being deprived of the thing they need most—perspective, to know why their parents behave so peculiarly and why their grandparents say the things they do.","cn":"年轻人被剥夺了他们最需要的东西——看待问题的视角，也就是了解为什么父母的行为如此古怪，以及为什么祖父母会说出那些话。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2020-12-1","level":"CET6","exam":"2020_12_1","year":2020,"month":12,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2020年12月 六级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2020年12月 CET-6 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet6-2020-12-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Good morning, Safe House Insurance.","cn":"M: 早上好，这里是 Safe House Insurance。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"My name is Paul.","cn":"我叫保罗。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"How can I help you today?","cn":"今天有什么可以帮您的吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Morning. I wouldn't say that it's good from where I am standing. This is Miss Wilson and this is the third time I've called this week since receiving your letter about our insurance claim. I'm getting a little fed up with my calls about my claim being completely disregarded.","cn":"W: 早上好。从我的处境来看，我可不觉得这是个美好的早晨。我是威尔逊女士。自从收到你们关于我们保险理赔的信以来，这是我本周第三次打电话了。我对你们完全不理会我关于理赔的来电，已经有点受够了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Miss Wilson, thank you for calling back.","cn":"M: 威尔逊女士，谢谢您再次来电。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Can I take some details to help me look at your claim?","cn":"我可以先记录一些信息，以便查看您的理赔情况吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: It's Miss May Wilson of 15 South Sea Road in Cornwall, and the details are that our village was extensively flooded 2 months ago. The entire ground floor of our cottage was submerged in water and five of us have been living in a caravan ever since. You people are still withholding the money we are entitled to over a bizarre technical detail. And it's not acceptable, Paul!","cn":"W: 我是康沃尔郡南海路15号的梅·威尔逊女士。事情是这样的：两个月前，我们的村子遭遇了严重洪水。我们小屋的整个底层都被水淹没了，我们五个人从那以后一直住在一辆拖车里。你们还在因为一个荒唐的技术细节，扣着我们应得的赔款不肯支付。这不可接受，保罗！"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Miss Wilson, according to the notes on your account, the bizarre technical detail that you mentioned refers to the fact that you hadn't paid house insurance the month before the incident.","cn":"M: 威尔逊女士，根据您账户上的记录，您提到的那个荒唐的技术细节，是指在事故发生前的那个月，您没有支付房屋保险费。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: That money left our account, and now that you should be paying out, you're suddenly saying that you didn't receive it on time.","cn":"W: 那笔钱已经从我们的账户里扣走了，而现在到了你们该赔付的时候，你们却突然说没有及时收到这笔钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'm really skeptical about this claim.","cn":"我真的对这次理赔感到怀疑。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: The contract does say that any missed payment in a year will affect the terms and conditions of the insurance contract and may affect claims.","cn":"M: 合同确实规定，一年中任何一次漏缴都会影响保险合同的条款和条件，并可能影响理赔。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Of course, I can pass you on to my manager to talk to you more about this.","cn":"当然，我可以把电话转给我的经理，让他就此事与您进一步沟通。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I've already spoken to him, and you can tell him I'm furious now, and that your company has a lawsuit on its hands.","cn":"W: 我已经和他谈过了，你可以告诉他，我现在非常愤怒，而且你们公司马上就要面临一场诉讼了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"You will be hearing from my lawyer.","cn":"你们会收到我律师的通知。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Goodbye.","cn":"再见。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: How do you feel about the future of artificial intelligence?","cn":"W: 你怎么看人工智能的未来？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Personally, I feel quite optimistic about it.","cn":"就我个人而言，我对此相当乐观。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: AI?","cn":"M: 人工智能？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm not so optimistic actually.","cn":"其实我没那么乐观。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"In fact, it's something we should be concerned about.","cn":"事实上，这是我们应该担心的事情。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Well, it will help us humans understand ourselves better.","cn":"W: 嗯，它会帮助我们人类更好地了解自己。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And, when we have a better understanding of ourselves, we can improve the world.","cn":"而当我们更了解自己时，就能改善这个世界。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, one thing is for sure: Technology is evolving faster than our ability to understand it.","cn":"M: 嗯，有一点是肯定的：科技发展的速度已经超过了我们理解它的能力。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And in the future, AI will make jobs kind of pointless.","cn":"而在未来，人工智能会让工作变得有些毫无意义。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I think artificial intelligence will actually help create new kinds of jobs, which would require less of our time and allow us to be centered on creative tasks.","cn":"W: 我认为人工智能实际上会帮助创造出新类型的工作，这些工作占用我们的时间会更少，也能让我们专注于创造性的任务。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I doubt that very much.","cn":"M: 我对此非常怀疑。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Probably the last job that will remain will be writing AI software.","cn":"可能最后会保留下来的工作就是编写人工智能软件。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And then eventually, AI will just write its own software.","cn":"然后最终，人工智能会编写自己的软件。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: At that time, we're going to have a lot of jobs which nobody will want to do, so we'll need artificial intelligence for the robots to take care of the old guys, like us.","cn":"W: 到那时，我们会有很多没人愿意做的工作，所以我们需要人工智能让机器人来照顾老人，比如我们这样的老人。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I don't know.","cn":"M: 我不知道。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"There's a risk that human civilization could be replaced by a superior type of digital life.","cn":"人类文明有可能被一种更高级的数字生命所取代。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"AI will be able to completely simulate a person in every way possible.","cn":"人工智能将能够以各种可能的方式完全模拟一个人。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"In fact, some people think we are in the simulation, right now.","cn":"事实上，有些人认为我们现在就处在一个模拟世界里。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That's impossible. Humans can't even make a mosquito. Computers only have chips. People have brains, and that's where the wisdom comes from.","cn":"W: 那不可能。人类甚至连一只蚊子都造不出来。计算机只有芯片，而人有大脑，智慧就来自那里。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Once it's fully developed, AI will become tired of trying to communicate with humans, as we would be much slower thinkers in comparison.","cn":"M: 一旦人工智能得到充分发展，它就会厌倦尝试与人类交流，因为相比之下，我们的思维速度会慢得多。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I'm not so sure.","cn":"W: 我不太确定。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"A computer is a computer, and a computer is just a toy.","cn":"计算机就是计算机，而计算机只不过是个玩具。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Computers can easily communicate incredibly fast, so the computer will just get impatient talking to humans.","cn":"M: 计算机可以非常轻松地以极快的速度交流，所以计算机和人类交谈时只会变得不耐烦。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It will be barely getting any information out.","cn":"它几乎得不到什么信息。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Well, I believe there is a benevolent future with AI.","cn":"W: 嗯，我相信人工智能会带来一个美好的未来。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I also think you watch too many science fiction films.","cn":"我还觉得你看了太多科幻电影。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"To achieve financial security, how much you save is always more important than the amount you earn or how shrewdly you invest.","cn":"要实现财务安全，你储蓄的金额始终比你的收入多少或投资有多精明更为重要。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"If you are under 30 years old, your goal should be to save 20% of your monthly income after tax deductions.","cn":"如果你未满30岁，你的目标应当是在扣除税款后，将月收入的20%存下来。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This is irrespective of how much you earn.","cn":"这与收入多少无关。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Approximately 50% should be reserved for essentials like food and accommodation.","cn":"大约50%应留作食物和住宿等基本生活开支。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The remaining 30% is for recreation and entertainment.","cn":"剩下的30%用于休闲和娱乐。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But for many young people, it'll be difficult to designate such a large proportion of their income for savings.","cn":"但是，对许多年轻人来说，将如此大比例的收入用于储蓄会很困难。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"If you find it hard to save any money at all, start by cutting all unnecessary spending.","cn":"如果你发现自己连一点钱都很难存下来，就先从削减所有不必要的开支开始。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Allocate a tiny amount of 1 or 2 percent for savings, and gradually increase that amount.","cn":"拿出一小部分收入，也就是1%或2%，用于储蓄，然后逐步提高这一比例。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Always keep that 20% goal in mind to prevent yourself from becoming complacent.","cn":"始终牢记20%的目标，以免自己变得安于现状。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It can be challenging to stick to such a strict plan, but if you adopt the right mindset, you should be able to make it work for you.","cn":"坚持这样严格的计划可能颇具挑战，但如果你采取正确的心态，就应该能够让它为你发挥作用。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So, what should you be doing with the money that you're saving?","cn":"那么，你应该如何使用正在储蓄的钱呢？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Some must be kept easily accessible in case you need some cash in an emergency.","cn":"其中一部分必须放在容易取用的地方，以备紧急情况下需要现金。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The largest proportion should be invested in retirement plans, either through your employer or privately.","cn":"最大的一部分应当投资于退休计划，可以通过雇主进行，也可以自行投资。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"And you can keep some money for high-risk but potentially lucrative investments.","cn":"你还可以留出一部分资金，用于高风险但可能带来丰厚收益的投资。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Dividends can be reinvested or used to purchase something you like.","cn":"股息可以再投资，也可以用来购买你喜欢的东西。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"By following this plan, you should hopefully be able to enjoy your life now, and still be financially secure in the future.","cn":"遵循这一计划，你应该有望既享受当下的生活，又在未来保持财务安全。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"I work in advertising and I like to keep up with current trends, mainly because I'm aware that we live in an image-obsessed world.","cn":"我从事广告行业，喜欢跟上当前的潮流，主要是因为我意识到我们生活在一个痴迷于外表的世界里。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"However, when I first started my job, occasionally I'd catch a glimpse of myself in the lifts, and find myself thinking that I looked a total mess.","cn":"不过，刚开始工作时，我偶尔会在电梯里瞥见自己，然后发现自己觉得自己看起来一团糟。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Was I being held back by my choice of clothing?","cn":"我的着装选择是否阻碍了我的发展？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The short answer is yes, especially when clients are quick to judge you on your style rather than your work.","cn":"简短的答案是“是”，尤其是当客户很快就会根据你的风格而不是你的工作来评判你时。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But no one can be unique with their outfit every day. I mean, that's why uniforms were invented. So, here's what I did. I created my own uniform. To do this, I chose an appropriate outfit. Then I bought multiple items of the same style in different shades. Now, I never worry about what I'm wearing in the morning even if I do get a bit tired of just wearing the same classic pieces.","cn":"但是，没有人能每天都穿出与众不同的服装。我的意思是，这就是制服被发明出来的原因。所以，我采取了这样的做法：我为自己设计了一套制服。为此，我选择了一套合适的服装，然后购买了多件不同色调的同款服饰。现在，我早上再也不用担心该穿什么了，尽管总是穿同样的经典款式确实会让我有些厌倦。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Overall, when it comes to work, you have to ask yourself: will looking smarter enhance my ability to do my job? For some, this question may not be an issue at all. Especially if you work remotely and rarely see your colleagues or clients face to face. But if your job involves interacting with other people, the answer to this is often yes. So rather than fighting the system, I think we should just do whatever helps us to achieve our goals at work. If that means playing it safe with your image, then let's face it. It's probably worth it.","cn":"总的来说，说到工作，你必须问问自己：看起来更得体会增强我的工作能力吗？对有些人来说，这个问题根本不成问题，尤其是当你远程工作，很少与同事或客户面对面交流时。但如果你的工作需要与他人互动，答案通常是肯定的。所以，我认为，与其对抗这种规则，不如做一切有助于我们在工作中实现目标的事情。如果这意味着在外表上采取稳妥的做法，那我们就面对现实吧。这可能是值得的。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Did you know that Americans have approximately three times the amount of space we had 50 years ago?","cn":"你知道吗，美国人如今拥有的空间大约是50年前的三倍。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Therefore, you'd think we'd have sufficient room for all of our possessions.","cn":"因此，你可能会认为，我们应该有足够的空间容纳所有个人物品。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"On the contrary, the personal storage business is now a growing industry.","cn":"然而事实恰恰相反，个人储物业务如今正成为一个不断发展的行业。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"We've got triple the space, but we've become such enthusiastic consumers that we require even more.","cn":"我们的空间增加了三倍，但我们已经成了如此热衷消费的人，以至于还需要更多空间。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This phenomenon has resulted in significant credit card debt, enormous environmental footprints, and perhaps not coincidentally, our happiness levels have failed to increase over the same half century.","cn":"这一现象导致了严重的信用卡债务和巨大的环境足迹，而且或许并非巧合，在这半个世纪里，我们的幸福感并没有随之提升。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"I'm here to suggest an alternative: having less might actually be a preferable decision.","cn":"我想在此提出另一种选择：拥有更少的东西实际上可能是更好的决定。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Many of us have experienced, at some stage, the pleasure of possessing less.","cn":"我们中的许多人都曾在人生的某个阶段体验过拥有更少物品所带来的快乐。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"I propose that less stuff and less space can not only help you economize, but also simplify your life.","cn":"我认为，减少物品和空间不仅能帮助你节省开支，还能简化你的生活。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"I recently started an innovative project to discover some creative solutions that offered me everything I required.","cn":"最近，我启动了一个创新项目，旨在寻找一些能满足我全部需求的创意解决方案。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"By purchasing an apartment that was 40 square meters instead of 60, I immediately saved $200,000.","cn":"我购买了一套40平方米而不是60平方米的公寓，立即节省了20万美元。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Smaller space leads to reduced utility bills, and also a smaller carbon footprint.","cn":"空间更小意味着更低的水电费，也意味着更小的碳足迹。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Because it is designed around an edited collection of possessions, limited to my favorite stuff, I'm really excited to live there.","cn":"由于这套公寓是围绕一组经过筛选、仅限于我最喜爱物品的收藏来设计的，我非常期待住在那里。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"How can we live more basically? Firstly, we must ruthlessly cut the unnecessary objects out of our lives. To stem consumption, we should think before we buy, and ask ourselves, \"Will it truly make me happier?\" Obviously, we should possess some great stuff, but we want belongings that we're going to love for years.","cn":"我们怎样才能过得更加简朴？首先，我们必须毫不留情地从生活中剔除不必要的物品。为了遏制消费，我们应该在购买之前先思考，并问自己：“它真的会让我更快乐吗？”当然，我们应该拥有一些很棒的物品，但我们希望拥有的是那些我们会喜爱多年的东西。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Secondly, we require space efficiency.","cn":"其次，我们需要提高空间利用效率。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"We want appliances that are designed for use most of the time, not for occasional use.","cn":"我们想要的是那些为大多数时间的使用而设计的电器，而不是只供偶尔使用的电器。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Why own a six-burner stove when you rarely use even three burners?","cn":"既然你连三个炉头都很少同时使用，为什么还要拥有一台六炉头的炉灶呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Finally, we need multifunctional spaces and housewares. I combined a movable wall with transforming furniture to get more out of my limited space. Consider my coffee table. It increases in size to accommodate ten. My office is tucked away, easily hidden. My bed simply pops out of the wall. For guests, I can relocate the movable wall and utilize the foldable guest beds I installed.","cn":"最后，我们需要多功能空间和家居用品。我把一面可移动的墙与可变形家具结合起来，以便更充分地利用有限的空间。以我的咖啡桌为例，它可以扩大，以容纳十个人。我的办公室收纳在隐蔽处，可以轻松藏起来。我的床只需从墙里弹出即可。来客人时，我可以移动那面墙，并使用我安装好的折叠式客床。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"I'm not saying we should all live in tiny apartments, but consider the benefits of an edited life. When you return home and walk through your front door, take a moment to ask yourselves, \"Could I do with a little life editing? Would that give me more freedom and more time?\"","cn":"我并不是说我们都应该住在小公寓里，但请想一想精简生活的好处。当你回到家，走过前门时，花一点时间问问自己：“我是否可以对生活做些删减？这样会不会让我拥有更多自由和时间？”"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Now, believe it or not, people sometimes lie in order to maintain a good, honest reputation—even if it hurts them to do so.","cn":"信不信由你，人们有时会为了维护良好、诚实的声誉而撒谎，即使这样做会让他们蒙受损失。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"At least, this is what a team of scientists is suggesting, with evidence to prove it.","cn":"至少，一组科学家提出了这一观点，并且有证据支持他们的说法。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Picture this scenario: You often drive for work and can be compensated for up to 400 miles per month.","cn":"设想一下这种情形：你经常因工作需要开车，每月最多可以报销400英里的里程。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Most people at your company drive about 300 miles each month.","cn":"你所在公司的大多数人每月开车约300英里。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But this month, you drove 400 miles.","cn":"但这个月，你开了400英里。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"How many miles do you think you'd claim in your expense report?","cn":"你认为自己会在费用报销单上申报多少英里？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The scientists asked this exact question as part of the study we're discussing today.","cn":"作为我们今天要讨论的这项研究的一部分，科学家们提出了这个一模一样的问题。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"With surprising results, they found that 12% of respondents reported the distance they drove as less than the actual figure, giving an average answer of 384 miles.","cn":"结果令人惊讶：他们发现，12%的受访者报告的驾驶距离低于实际数值，平均回答为384英里。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In other words, they lied about the number of miles, even though they would forfeit money they were owed.","cn":"换句话说，他们谎报了驾驶里程，尽管这意味着他们会放弃本应得到的钱。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The researchers believe this was to seem honest, with the assumption being that others would be suspicious of a high expense claim.","cn":"研究人员认为，这样做是为了显得诚实，因为他们假定别人会对高额费用申报产生怀疑。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But why would people fabricate numbers to their own detriment?","cn":"但人们为什么要捏造数字，让自己蒙受损失呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The researchers explain that many people care a great deal about their reputation and how they'll be judged by others.","cn":"研究人员解释说，许多人非常在意自己的声誉，以及别人会如何评价自己。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"If they care enough, their concern about appearing honest and not losing the respect of others may be greater than their desire to actually be honest.","cn":"如果这种在意程度足够高，那么他们对显得诚实以及不失去他人尊重的担忧，可能会超过他们真正做到诚实的愿望。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The researchers assert that the findings suggest that when people obtain very favorable outcomes, they anticipate other people's suspicious reactions and prefer lying and appearing honest to telling the truth and appearing as selfish liars.","cn":"研究人员断言，这些研究结果表明，当人们获得非常有利的结果时，他们会预料到他人产生怀疑的反应，并且更愿意撒谎、装作诚实，也不愿意说出真相、显得像自私的骗子。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"So why is this research important?","cn":"那么，这项研究为什么重要呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Well, experts generally agree there are two main types of lie-selfish lies and lies that are meant to benefit others.","cn":"一般来说，专家们认为谎言主要有两种类型：自私的谎言，以及旨在让他人受益的谎言。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The first, as you may predict, is for selfish gain, such as submitting a fraudulent claim to an insurance company, while the second involves lying to help others or not offend others, for example, telling a friend whose outfit you don't like that they look great.","cn":"第一种，正如你可能预料的那样，是为了谋取私利，例如向保险公司提交欺诈性索赔；第二种则是为了帮助他人或不冒犯他人而撒谎，例如告诉一个你不喜欢其穿着的朋友，他们看起来很棒。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But the researchers are suggesting a third type of lying—lying to maintain a good reputation.","cn":"但研究人员提出了第三种撒谎类型，即为了维护良好声誉而撒谎。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Now this hypothesis is new and some skeptics argue that this isn't a whole new category of lie.","cn":"这个假设是新的，一些怀疑论者认为，这并不是一种全新的谎言类别。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But the findings seem intuitive to me.","cn":"但在我看来，这些研究结果似乎很符合直觉。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"After all, one of the main motivations for lying is to increase our worth in the eyes of others.","cn":"毕竟，撒谎的主要动机之一，就是提升自己在他人眼中的价值。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"So it seems highly likely that people will lie to seem honest.","cn":"因此，人们很可能会为了显得诚实而撒谎。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Why do old people dislike new music?","cn":"为什么老年人不喜欢新音乐？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"As I've grown older, I often hear people my age say things like \"They just don't make good music like they used to\".","cn":"随着年龄增长，我经常听到和我年龄相仿的人说：“现在的音乐就是没有过去的好听。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Why does this happen?","cn":"”为什么会这样？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Luckily, psychology can give us some insights into this puzzle.","cn":"幸运的是，心理学可以为这个谜题提供一些见解。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Musical tastes begin to crystallize as early as age 13 or 14.","cn":"音乐品味早在十三四岁时就开始逐渐定型。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"By the time we're in our early 20s, these tastes get locked into place pretty firmly.","cn":"到了二十岁出头，这些品味通常已经相当牢固地固定下来。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In fact, studies have found that by the time we turn 33, most of us have stopped listening to new music.","cn":"事实上，研究发现，到我们三十三岁时，大多数人已经不再听新音乐了。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Meanwhile, popular songs released when you're in your early teens are likely to remain quite popular among your age group through the rest of your life.","cn":"与此同时，在你十几岁早期发行的流行歌曲，很可能会在你的年龄群体中一直保持相当高的人气，直至你一生的余下时光。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"There could be a biological explanation for this, as there's evidence that the brain's ability to make subtle distinctions between different chords, rhythms and melodies deteriorates with age.","cn":"对此可能存在一种生物学上的解释，因为有证据表明，随着年龄增长，大脑区分不同和弦、节奏和旋律之间细微差别的能力会逐渐衰退。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"So to older people, newer, less familiar songs might all \"sound the same\".","cn":"因此，对老年人来说，较新且不太熟悉的歌曲可能听起来都“一个样”。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But there may be some simpler reasons for older people's aversion to newer music.","cn":"但老年人排斥新音乐也可能有一些更简单的原因。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"One of the most researched laws of social psychology is something called the \"mere exposure effect\", which, in essence, means that the more we're exposed to something, the more we tend to like it.","cn":"社会心理学中研究最充分的规律之一被称为“纯粹接触效应”，其本质是，我们接触某种事物越多，就越倾向于喜欢它。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This happens with people we know, the advertisements we see and the songs we listen to.","cn":"我们对熟悉的人、所看到的广告以及所听的歌曲，都会产生这种效应。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"When you're in your early teens, you probably spend a fair amount of time listening to music or watching music videos.","cn":"十几岁早期时，你可能会花相当多的时间听音乐或看音乐视频。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Your favorite songs and artists become familiar, comforting parts of your routine.","cn":"你喜欢的歌曲和音乐人会逐渐成为日常生活中熟悉而令人感到安心的一部分。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"For many people over 30, job and family obligations increase, so there's less time to spend discovering new music.","cn":"对许多三十岁以上的人来说，工作和家庭责任增加了，因此用于发现新音乐的时间减少了。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Instead, many will simply listen to old, familiar favorites from that period of their lives when they had more free time.","cn":"相反，许多人会一直听那些熟悉的老歌，那些歌曲来自他们人生中拥有更多空闲时间的时期。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Of course, those teen years weren't necessarily carefree.","cn":"当然，青少年时期并不一定无忧无虑。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They're famously confusing, which is why so many TV shows and movies revolve around high school turmoil.","cn":"这个阶段出了名地充满困惑，这也是为什么那么多电视节目和电影都围绕高中生活中的动荡展开。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Psychology research has shown that the emotions that we experience as teens seem more intense than those that come later.","cn":"心理学研究表明，我们在青少年时期体验到的情绪似乎比后来经历的情绪更加强烈。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And we also know that intense emotions are associated with stronger memories and preferences.","cn":"我们也知道，强烈的情绪与更深刻的记忆和更强烈的偏好有关。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Both of these might explain why the songs we listen to during this period become so memorable and beloved.","cn":"这两点都可能解释了为什么我们在这一时期听过的歌曲会变得如此令人难忘，并深受喜爱。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"So there's nothing wrong with your parents because they don't like your music.","cn":"所以，你的父母不喜欢你听的音乐，并不意味着他们有什么问题。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Rather it's all part of the natural order of things.","cn":"这只是事物自然规律的一部分。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2020-12-2","level":"CET6","exam":"2020_12_2","year":2020,"month":12,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2020年12月 六级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2020年12月 CET-6 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2020/cet6-2020-12-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: This is unbelievable.","cn":"W：这真是难以置信。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Unlike any video game I've ever played before, it's so boring, yet so relaxing at the same time.","cn":"它和我以前玩过的任何电子游戏都不一样，既无聊，却又让人感到放松。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"How did you hear about this driving simulator?","cn":"你是怎么听说这个驾驶模拟器的？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: My brother introduced it to me last year.","cn":"M：我哥哥去年介绍给我的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I was surprised to find how educational and realistic it was.","cn":"我很惊讶地发现它既有教育意义，又非常逼真。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's called Euro Truck Simulator, but they have other versions as well for America and so on.","cn":"它叫《欧洲卡车模拟》，不过他们也有美国版之类的其他版本。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I was really drawn to the scenery.","cn":"我真的很喜欢里面的风景。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The routes go through parts of the country you don't normally see as a tourist.","cn":"路线会经过一些游客通常不会去的地方。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Yeah, I can see that.","cn":"W：是啊，我能看出来。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It seems so simple, just transporting cargo from point A to point B, driving from one city to another.","cn":"它看起来很简单，就是把货物从A点运到B点，从一个城市开到另一个城市。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I really appreciate all the details that go into the game.","cn":"但我真的很欣赏这款游戏中的各种细节。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's even given me a new appreciation for the logistics industry and traffic on the road.","cn":"它甚至让我开始更加了解物流行业以及道路上的交通状况。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I completely agree.","cn":"M：我完全同意。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"My brother also introduced me to some videos of someone that streams their game online.","cn":"我哥哥还给我介绍了一些视频，视频里有人在网上直播玩这个游戏。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It was fascinating to watch, really.","cn":"看起来真的很有意思。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This guy drove very carefully, obeyed all the road signs and traffic rules—such a contrast to most violent games.","cn":"那个人开车非常小心，遵守所有道路标志和交通规则，这和大多数暴力游戏形成了鲜明对比。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Honestly, playing has inspired me to look into the industry more.","cn":"W：说实话，玩这个游戏让我产生了进一步了解这个行业的想法。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I've read articles about how self-driving trucks may soon be available and could greatly impact cargo logistics.","cn":"我读过一些文章，说自动驾驶卡车可能很快就会投入使用，并可能对货物运输产生重大影响。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Considering all that goes into driving these larger vehicles, it's amazing that we could soon have that kind of technology.","cn":"考虑到驾驶这些大型车辆需要处理的各种情况，我们很快就能拥有那样的技术，真是令人惊叹。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Ha. I've got one step further. I registered to take a safe driving course to improve my real-life driving skills. In a way, I feel like I have a head start compared to other students in the class. Playing this video game has given me some maneuvering practices already.","cn":"M：哈，我还更进一步。我报名参加了安全驾驶课程，想提高自己在现实生活中的驾驶技能。在某种程度上，我觉得与班上的其他学员相比，自己已经领先了一步。玩这款电子游戏已经让我练习了一些操控技巧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I'm not sure how accurate the video game is compared to real-life situations.","cn":"W：我不确定这款电子游戏与现实情况相比有多准确。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But if it results in more drivers looking both ways before entering an intersection, I'd say that's a positive outcome.","cn":"但如果它能让更多司机在驶入十字路口前先左右观察，我会说这是一种积极的结果。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: How do you like being self-employed?","cn":"W: 你喜欢做个体经营者吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: There are obvious benefits, though I don't seem to have the freedom I anticipated as I just don't seem able to decline work offers.","cn":"M: 这当然有明显的好处，不过我好像没有获得原本预想的自由，因为我似乎根本没法拒绝工作机会。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And working alone, there have been times when I've found that money alone provides insufficient motivation.","cn":"而且一个人工作时，我有时会发现，光靠钱并不足以提供动力。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Have you experienced the same since you began working for yourself?","cn":"自从你开始为自己工作以来，你也有过同样的经历吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Sometimes, yes.","cn":"W: 有时候，是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Unlike the rest of the workforce who have managers to prompt motivation whenever they're feeling lazy or bored, we self-employed workers perform our jobs without a manager to lift our spirits.","cn":"其他劳动者懒散或感到无聊时，会有经理来督促他们、激发他们的动力；而我们这些个体经营者没有经理来鼓舞士气，只能独自完成工作。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"There's no one around to offer praise or initiate collaboration, no one to make greater use of our interests and talents.","cn":"身边没有人给予表扬或发起合作，也没有人更充分地利用我们的兴趣和才能。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: That's a fact.","cn":"M: 确实如此。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Not every manager behaves with such awareness and care, of course.","cn":"当然，并不是每个经理都能如此体察下属、如此体贴。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And certainly not all managers have a clue how to motivate people.","cn":"而且，肯定也不是所有经理都知道该如何激励员工。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Still, having a manager nearby at least indicates there's an opportunity they'll be decent enough to look out for you when your energy and focus begin to deplete.","cn":"不过，身边有个经理，至少说明当你的精力和注意力开始消耗殆尽时，对方有可能足够体面，愿意照顾你。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: The motivator I value most is autonomy.","cn":"W: 我最看重的激励因素是自主性。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I've learned not to sacrifice my prized autonomy by working all hours of the day and by saying yes to every client request.","cn":"我已经学会了不为了整天工作、也不为了答应客户的每一个要求，而牺牲自己珍视的自主权。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yes.","cn":"M: 是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I need to remind myself that I selected this lifestyle for the independence.","cn":"我需要提醒自己，我选择这种生活方式就是为了独立。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I don't miss aspects of permanent full-time employment I disliked, such as the office politics, job insecurity, inflexible hours and so on.","cn":"我并不怀念那些我不喜欢的全职长期雇佣工作的方面，比如办公室政治、工作不稳定、工作时间不灵活等等。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I wouldn't mind a bit more in the form of praise though, praise which is on the record.","cn":"不过，如果能多得到一些表扬，我倒不会介意，尤其是正式记录在案的表扬。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That'll come with time.","cn":"W: 这会随着时间而来。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Relatedness is inevitably cultivated via human interaction.","cn":"人与人之间的互动必然会培养关系联结感。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Engaging with clients, getting written testimony and recommendations, staying in contact with clients afterwards, these are things you'll find will come in due course and provide you with motivation.","cn":"与客户交流、获得书面证明和推荐、之后继续与客户保持联系，这些事情你会发现都会逐渐出现，并为你提供动力。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: You're right.","cn":"M: 你说得对。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"That's an area I do need to put some more effort into—building closer relationships with those who engage my services and skills.","cn":"这方面我确实需要多下些功夫，也就是和那些聘用我的服务和技能的人建立更亲密的关系。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Weather is a constant force in our lives, but there is little marketing research on how it affects businesses.","cn":"天气是我们生活中持续存在的一股力量，但关于天气如何影响企业的营销研究却很少。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Now, a new study reveals how sunny and snowy conditions influence consumer behavior.","cn":"如今，一项新研究揭示了晴朗和下雪的天气状况如何影响消费者行为。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Those weather conditions trigger consumers to mentally visualize using products associated with the respective weather.","cn":"这些天气状况会促使消费者在脑海中想象使用与相应天气相关的产品。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This leads to consumers placing a higher value on those products.","cn":"这会使消费者更加看重这些产品。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"That is, they're willing to pay more money for them.","cn":"也就是说，他们愿意为这些产品支付更多的钱。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But the correlation is only found with products related to being outside.","cn":"但这种相关性仅存在于与户外活动有关的产品中。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"How does this work?","cn":"这是如何起作用的呢？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers give the example of a beach towel.","cn":"研究人员以沙滩巾为例。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"On a sunny day, consumers who see that product are not just looking at the towel itself, they are likely imagining themselves lying on the towel in the sun.","cn":"在晴天，看到这件产品的消费者不只是看着沙滩巾本身，他们很可能会想象自己躺在阳光下的沙滩巾上。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This mental picture of using the towel increases the value of the product in the consumers' mind.","cn":"这样一幅使用沙滩巾的心理画面，会提高消费者心目中这件产品的价值。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers put forward the following hypothesis to explain their findings.","cn":"研究人员提出了以下假设来解释他们的发现。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"They think the mental picture works in sunshine and snow because these weather conditions have a positive association with outside activities.","cn":"他们认为，阳光和雪天之所以会产生这种心理画面，是因为这些天气状况与户外活动之间存在积极联系。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The effect is not seen with rainy weather.","cn":"下雨天气则不会产生这种影响。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers assert this is because there aren't many activities that are enabled by rain.","cn":"研究人员认为，这是因为雨天能开展的活动并不多。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Most products associated with rain, like umbrellas, are only used for protection from the weather, and not for any activities.","cn":"大多数与下雨有关的产品，如雨伞，都只是用来抵御天气影响，而不是用于进行任何活动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers believe that companies that sell a wide array of products online can benefit most from the insights this study provides.","cn":"研究人员认为，在线销售种类繁多产品的公司最能从这项研究提供的洞见中受益。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Online sellers often use complex mathematical formulas to determine what products to feature and how to price these products.","cn":"在线卖家通常会使用复杂的数学公式来确定重点展示哪些产品以及如何为这些产品定价。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Incorporating more data about weather would allow them to make better decisions.","cn":"纳入更多有关天气的数据，将使他们能够作出更好的决策。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This could bolster sales.","cn":"这可能会促进销售。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Setting the office air-conditioning at about 22℃ has become standard practice across the world.","cn":"将办公室空调设定在约22摄氏度，已成为世界各地的惯例。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Numerous guidebooks across the world on heating, ventilation and air-conditioning claim office performance peaks at 22 degrees.","cn":"世界各地众多有关供暖、通风和空调的指南都声称，办公室工作效率在22摄氏度时达到最高。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Many people indeed find relief from soaring summer temperatures in air-conditioned offices.","cn":"事实上，许多人确实能在装有空调的办公室里缓解夏季高温带来的不适。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But recent studies have challenged the accepted wisdom that a cool office is more productive.","cn":"然而，近期研究对“凉爽的办公室能提高工作效率”这一公认观点提出了质疑。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The reality is more complex.","cn":"实际情况更加复杂。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Researchers conducted a review of all studies relating to air-conditioning and productivity.","cn":"研究人员对所有涉及空调与工作效率的研究进行了综述。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"They found that 22 degrees was probably a little chilly, even at the height of summer.","cn":"他们发现，即使在盛夏，22摄氏度可能也有些凉。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For a person dressed in typical summer clothing, an optimal range would be between 23 and 26 degrees.","cn":"对于穿着典型夏装的人来说，最佳温度范围应在23至26摄氏度之间。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"And people can even tolerate temperatures beyond this comfort zone as long as they can adjust their clothing and expectations.","cn":"只要人们能够调整衣着和心理预期，他们甚至可以忍受超过这一舒适区的温度。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In fact, even on very hot days, it makes sense to turn the air-conditioning up.","cn":"事实上，即使在非常炎热的日子里，把空调温度调高也是合理的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"People often chase just one optimum temperature, and this is understandable when people feel hot.","cn":"人们往往只追求一个最佳温度，当人感到炎热时，这种做法是可以理解的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But there is a range of at least three to four degrees which does not have any adverse impact.","cn":"但实际上，存在一个至少三到四摄氏度的温度范围，在这个范围内，工作效率不会受到任何不利影响。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Another issue related to this is that people can become psychologically dependent on air conditioning. If they're used to the environment which is air-conditioned, they tend to prefer lower temperatures. But the studies found that almost all humans became accustomed to the new temperature. It was only at the extreme ends of the temperature range where people's productivity suffered. This range was above 26 degrees and below 19 degrees.","cn":"与此相关的另一个问题是，人们可能会在心理上依赖空调。如果人们习惯了有空调的环境，就会倾向于偏好较低的温度。但研究发现，几乎所有人都能适应新的温度。只有在温度范围的两端，也就是高于26摄氏度或低于19摄氏度时，人们的工作效率才会受到影响。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Psychology research has tended to portray solitude as a negative experience.","cn":"心理学研究往往将独处描绘成一种负面体验。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Studies conducted in the 1970s and 1990s suggested that people felt less happy when alone as compared to being with others.","cn":"20世纪70年代和90年代开展的研究表明，与和他人在一起相比，人们独处时感到不那么快乐。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"However, a new paper shows an alternative view of solitude, one in which solitude can be positive.","cn":"然而，一篇新的论文展现了关于独处的另一种观点，认为独处也可以是积极的。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Let's start by looking at the earlier research. It had a couple of shortcomings. First, it measured emotion on a scale from positive to negative, overlooking the possibility that our positive and negative emotions can fluctuate independently. Also, it categorized emotions as simply positive or negative. It didn't consider that emotions arouse us to different degrees, and that both positive and negative emotions can arouse us a lot or a little. That is, whether positive or negative, emotions can be either high-arousal or low-arousal. High-arousal emotions include excitement on the positive side or anger on the negative side, while low-arousal ones include feeling calm on the positive side or lonely on the negative.","cn":"我们先来看看早期的研究。这些研究存在几个缺陷。首先，它们用从积极到消极的尺度来衡量情绪，忽视了积极情绪和消极情绪可能各自独立波动的可能性。此外，它们只是将情绪归类为积极或消极，没有考虑到情绪会以不同程度唤起我们，而且积极情绪和消极情绪都可能具有较高或较低的唤起程度。也就是说，无论是积极情绪还是消极情绪，都可能属于高唤起或低唤起情绪。高唤起情绪包括积极方面的兴奋，也包括消极方面的愤怒；低唤起情绪则包括积极方面的平静感，也包括消极方面的孤独感。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This new research attempted to overcome these shortcomings.","cn":"这项新研究试图克服这些缺陷。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Researchers began with a simple study.","cn":"研究人员首先进行了一项简单的研究。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"They asked participants to spend 15 minutes sitting alone without engaging in any activity, and measured how this solitude influences their emotional state.","cn":"他们要求参与者独自坐着15分钟，不从事任何活动，并测量独处如何影响他们的情绪状态。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This experiment specifically aimed to determine the effect of solitude on high-arousal emotions.","cn":"这项实验旨在确定独处对高唤起情绪的影响。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It looked at positive emotions such as being excited or interested, and negative emotions including being scared or distressed.","cn":"研究考察了兴奋或感兴趣等积极情绪，也考察了害怕或痛苦等消极情绪。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The results were clear.","cn":"结果很明确。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"After 15 minutes of solitude, the participants showed reductions in both types of emotion.","cn":"独处15分钟后，参与者的这两类情绪都有所减弱。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"A second study measured the effects of solitude on low-arousal emotions.","cn":"第二项研究测量了独处对低唤起情绪的影响。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"These included both positive and negative emotions, such as feeling calm, relaxed, sad or lonely.","cn":"这些情绪既包括积极情绪，也包括消极情绪，例如平静、放松、悲伤或孤独感。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"That experiment found that all of these emotions were increased by time alone.","cn":"实验发现，独处时间的增加使所有这些情绪都增强了。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Thus it seems past depictions of solitude were wrong.","cn":"因此，过去对独处的描述似乎是错误的。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It doesn't have a simple emotional effect that can be characterized as good or bad.","cn":"独处并不会产生一种可以简单归为好或坏的情绪影响。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Rather, it changes the intensity of our inner experience.","cn":"相反，它会改变我们内在体验的强度。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It amplifies quieter emotions, but it diminishes the intensity of stronger feelings.","cn":"它会放大较为微弱的情绪，却会减弱较强烈感受的强度。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It's worth clarifying that these findings relate to relatively brief periods of solitude.","cn":"需要明确的是，这些发现与相对较短时间的独处有关。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This is distinct from prolonged loneliness.","cn":"这不同于长期的孤独。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Research has demonstrated that the latter is correlated with an assortment of negative physical and psychological effects.","cn":"研究表明，后者与一系列负面的生理和心理影响相关。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"How can people benefit from being alone?","cn":"人们如何从独处中受益？"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The findings here suggest that people can use solitude to regulate their emotions.","cn":"这里的研究结果表明，人们可以利用独处来调节情绪。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Solitude can help us become quiet after excitement, calm after an angry episode, or simply feel at peace.","cn":"独处可以帮助我们在兴奋之后安静下来，在愤怒发作之后平静下来，或者仅仅让我们感到内心平和。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In 1984, the World Chess Championship was called off abruptly, due to the withered frame of a player who was competing for the title.","cn":"1984年，世界国际象棋锦标赛因一名争夺冠军的棋手身体日渐消瘦而被突然叫停。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"He wasn't alone in experiencing the extreme physical effects of the game.","cn":"他并不是唯一一个在这项运动中经历极端身体影响的人。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Elite players can reportedly burn up to an absurd 6,000 calories in one day.","cn":"据报道，顶尖棋手一天最多可以燃烧多达荒谬的6000卡路里。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Does that mean that thinking harder is a simple route to losing weight?","cn":"这是否意味着，更加努力地思考就是一条简单的减肥途径？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Well, when the body is at rest, we know that the brain uses up a startling 20% to 25% of the body's overall energy.","cn":"那么，当身体处于静息状态时，我们知道大脑会消耗全身总能量的惊人20%至25%。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This level of utilization actually makes the brain the most energy-expensive organ in the body, and yet it makes up only 2% of the body's weight overall.","cn":"这种程度的能量利用实际上使大脑成为人体中能量消耗最高的器官，然而它的重量却只占人体总重量的2%。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"So the more we put this organ to work, the more calories we'll burn?","cn":"所以，我们越让这个器官运转，就会燃烧越多卡路里吗？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Technically, the answer is yes, for cognitively difficult tasks.","cn":"严格来说，对于认知难度较高的任务，答案是肯定的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"What counts as a \"difficult\" mental task varies between individuals.","cn":"对不同的人而言，什么算是“困难”的脑力任务各不相同。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But generally, it could be described as something that the brain cannot solve easily using previously learned routines, or tasks that change the conditions continuously.","cn":"但通常可以将其描述为：大脑无法利用此前学会的惯常方法轻易解决的事情，或者条件持续发生变化的任务。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"However, deep thinking will not burn off the calories gained from eating a sugary snack.","cn":"然而，深度思考并不能消耗掉吃甜食所摄入的卡路里。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Because in relation to the brain's huge overall energy usage, which is devoted to a multitude of tasks, the energy required just to think harder is actually comparatively tiny.","cn":"因为相对于大脑用于完成大量任务的巨大总体能量消耗而言，仅仅为了更加努力地思考所需的能量实际上微乎其微。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"We're unconscious of most of what uses up the brain's energy.","cn":"我们没有意识到大脑的大部分能量究竟消耗在了什么地方。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"A lot of that activity is unrelated to conscious activities like learning how to sing or play the guitar.","cn":"其中许多活动都与学习唱歌或弹吉他这类有意识的活动无关。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The brain is able to allocate blood (and thus energy) to particular regions that are being active at that point.","cn":"大脑能够将血液（因而也包括能量）分配到当时正在活动的特定区域。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But the overall energy availability in the brain is thought to be constant.","cn":"不过，人们认为大脑整体可利用的能量是恒定的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"So, while there might be significant increases in energy use at localized regions of the brain when we perform difficult cognitive tasks, when it comes to the whole brain's energy budget overall, these activities don't significantly alter it.","cn":"因此，当我们执行困难的认知任务时，大脑局部区域的能量使用量可能会显著增加，但就整个大脑的总体能量预算而言，这些活动并不会对其产生显著影响。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"So, why did the chess champion grow too skinny to compete in his chess competition?","cn":"那么，为什么那位国际象棋冠军会瘦到无法参加他的国际象棋比赛呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The general consensus is that it mostly comes down to stress and reduced food consumption, not mental exhaustion.","cn":"普遍的共识是，这主要归因于压力和食物摄入量减少，而不是精神疲劳。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Keeping your body pumped up for action for long periods of time is very energy demanding.","cn":"长时间让身体保持随时行动的状态会消耗大量能量。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"If you can't eat as often or as much as you can or would normally—then you might lose weight.","cn":"如果你无法像平时那样频繁进食，或者无法吃下平时那么多食物，那么你可能会体重下降。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"\"Tell me about yourself\" may seem like an easy job interview question, but the open-ended nature of this question often leaves job seekers at a loss where to start.","cn":"“介绍一下你自己”似乎是一个简单的面试问题，但这个问题的开放性往往让求职者不知从何说起。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This common question is actually a critical test of a job candidate's communication skills, so it's important not to give an unprepared response or mess it up.","cn":"这个常见问题实际上是对求职者沟通能力的一项重要考验，因此不要毫无准备地作答或把事情搞砸，这一点很重要。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"\"Tell me about yourself\" is often the first question professional career coaches prepare people for when they give interview guidance.","cn":"“介绍一下你自己”通常是专业职业教练在提供面试指导时，首先帮助人们准备的问题。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It's the opportunity for the candidate to take control of the narrative and tell their story in a way that really matters to their audience.","cn":"这是求职者掌控叙述、以一种真正对听众有意义的方式讲述自己经历的机会。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It takes hard work and extensive preparation to answer this question well.","cn":"要很好地回答这个问题，需要付出艰苦努力并进行充分准备。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"When a person goes to a job interview, their interviewer has presumably read their résumé, so they don't need to repeat the information.","cn":"一个人去参加求职面试时，面试官大概已经读过他的简历，因此他不需要重复其中的信息。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But that's what most people will do, as it's their instinct to recite things that are already on their résumé.","cn":"但大多数人都会这样做，因为他们本能地会复述简历上已经写有的内容。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It's important for job seekers to do their homework on two crucial aspects.","cn":"求职者有必要在两个关键方面做好准备。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"First, they are not just telling someone a fact about themselves.","cn":"首先，他们并不只是在告诉别人一个关于自己的事实，而是在讲述一个故事，而故事需要花费心力来构思。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They're telling a story, and stories take work to create.","cn":"想出一个好故事，意味着要反思：是什么让他们的职业成就成为令自己感到自豪的事情，以及这些成就凸显了哪些优势。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Coming up with a good story means getting reflective about what made their career accomplishments something they're proud of and what strengths those accomplishments highlight.","cn":"求职者不应挑选一个宽泛的、笼统的优势来展开，例如“我很聪明，我工作努力，而且我能把事情办成”。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Candidates shouldn't pick a broad general strength to elaborate on, such as \"I'm smart, I work hard and I get things done.\" To come up with multiple career accomplishments or examples for different interview questions, job seekers should talk with others, especially people who know them, partners, friends or co-workers who will bring up different stories than the ones they remember.","cn":"为了针对不同的面试问题想出多个职业成就或事例，求职者应该与他人交谈，尤其是那些了解自己的人、伴侣、朋友或同事，因为他们会提起一些与求职者记得的不同的故事。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Secondly, candidates should know what's at stake for the company with this job opening. What they really are asking you is \"Tell me why you are going to help me.\" If the person is a prepared candidate, they should have already figured out those things. They've read the job description and researched the company on the Internet. What job applicants ought to be looking for is what the company is up to, what they are trying to accomplish and what is preventing them from accomplishing those things.","cn":"其次，求职者应该了解公司在招聘这个职位时所面临的利害关系。公司真正想问的是：“告诉我，你为什么能帮助我。”如果求职者准备充分，就应该已经弄清楚这些问题。他们读过职位描述，也在互联网上研究过这家公司。求职者应该关注的是：公司正在做什么、试图实现什么，以及是什么阻碍了他们实现这些目标。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"How long should it take to answer?","cn":"回答需要多长时间？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Around a minute.","cn":"大约一分钟。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"That's about right for most people's attention spans.","cn":"对于大多数人的注意力持续时间来说，这个时长比较合适。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Under a minute could seem rushed, while over two minutes will start to feel more like a speech.","cn":"不到一分钟可能会显得过于仓促，而超过两分钟就会开始更像是在演讲。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But the length of the answer is not an exact science, and candidates need to keep their career story focused and tailored to their audience.","cn":"但答案的长度并没有绝对标准，求职者需要让自己的职业经历叙述保持重点突出，并根据听众进行调整。"}]}];
